ch `APPEND_ONLY` member removed from the tuple → that key's own `--set …=[]` fixture,\n    run with that key alone, which expects exit 2 and an unchanged store.\n  - v1.0's row \"`--append` mutating the prior list in place\" is dropped: the prior record is\n    discarded after the write, so the persisted bytes are identical in both modes and no\n    observation the suite makes can see it (codex audit cycle 1, run on a controlled pair).\n  - The `independent` consistency check removed → a lying-boolean fixture.\n1440→  - The `unrecorded` trigger restricted to `implementer == \"agy\"` → the `codex` fixture (AC-7.2).\n  - A malformed 6a-prime entry counted as recorded → its fixture.\n  - The `unrecorded` detail text reading `implementer_switch.to` → the switch/recovery fixture.\n  - `property_valid`'s `dict` guard removed (the predicate applied to `value[\"ts\"]` directly) →\n    `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)`, which then raises.\n- **FR-9:** the 8 + 2 rows in §\"FR-9\".\n\n**Existing rows the edits move (E7).** The rule over the class: after each Task, every committed\nmutation row whose `file` the Task edits must still match its `find` exactly once\n(`h_mad_mutation_harness.py --check-anchors`, the harness's own `source.count(find)` test), and a\n1450→row the edit breaks is re-anchored **in that Task**, to the same intent and the same `test`. The\nsweep that found them: every row of `h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/*.json` whose `file` is one this\ndesign edits outside FR-3's and FR-6's files (which §\"FR-3\" and §\"FR-6\" already re-anchor\nwhole), with each `find` located in the file at `cff71b49`:\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `w10a-grok-by-default` (FR-5 Task): its `find` is the `--agent`\n  choices line, which FR-5 rewrites. Re-anchor: `find`\n  `ap.add_argument(\"--agent\", choices=(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\"), default=\"codex\")`, `replace` the\n  same with `default=\"grok\"`, `test` unchanged.\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `t1-timeout-judged-by-value` (FR-5 Task): `find`\n  `args.timeout is not None` sits on the timeout line FR-5 rewrites; the line form in §\"FR-5\"\n1460→  keeps it once, and the `replace` (`args.timeout not in (None, 900)`) still bites\n  `test_agent_grok_explicit_timeout_wins`. No re-anchor if that form is kept.\n- `grok_wire_reverts.json` `wr3-assembler-drops-agent` (FR-5 Task): `find` `        agent=args.agent,`\n  must stay once; the check run FR-5 adds to `main` must not repeat that line.\n- `heartbeat_beat.json` `the-owners-set-no-longer-beats` and `a-bystanders-set-beats-too` (FR-7\n  Task): `find` is `merge_fields`' owner-heartbeat `if` and its assignment; §\"FR-7\" keeps both\n  byte for byte, so no re-anchor. The other two rows of that spec anchor in `beat`, which FR-7\n  does not edit.\n- SKILL.md and `failure-recovery.md` rows: none of their `find` texts lies in a span FR-9/FR-10\n  rewrites (the nearest are `phase7_integrate_blockers_documented.json`'s three rows inside Phase 7\n1470→  item 7 (the closure list, around its 7f integrate step), which the item-7 edit only adds to, and\n  `baseline_sha.json`/`wire_registry_key.json` in §\"Phase 5 (Implementation) sub-steps\" on the 5f\n  bullet, not the 5d bullet FR-9 edits). Every other row on\n  `h_mad_assemble_tdd.py`, `h_mad_state_write.py`, `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` and\n  `h_mad_hook_wiring.py` anchors on code this design does not rewrite. `h_mad_state_validate.py`,\n  `h_mad_state_schema.json` and `codex-implementer-prompt.md` have no rows.\nResidual: the sweep reads the design's edit sites as described here; an implementation that\nrewrites more than it describes moves rows this list does not name, which `--check-anchors` then\ncatches in that Task.\n\n1480→## Residuals\n\nEach is stated where it arises. Collected here:\n- the `which` / `command -v` matrix (FR-2);\n- the verb reads the root only (FR-2);\n- the class-(a) judgement (FR-4);\n- the six-line shell composition in both gates (FR-4);\n- a sibling `overwrite` (FR-4);\n- the review-leg agy is gated too (FR-4);\n- worktree state, not claimed either way (FR-4);\n1490→- an equivalent command spelling (FR-5);\n- a writer that bypasses `_mutate` (FR-7);\n- the deliberate differences from the Codex gate's target sequence, and any rule it gains later\n  (FR-4);\n- relative shell tokens under a `Cwd` that does not exist (FR-4);\n- code a reviewer wrote outside an implementation dispatch (FR-7);\n- prose application (FR-9);\n- a contradicting sentence or a seventh surface (FR-9);\n- (v1.2) a judge kind added to `KINDS` later passes through unlisted (FR-4);\n- (v1.2) T4's empty-string arm is an equivalent mutant, unpinned (Mutation rows);\n1500→- (v1.2) a module missing its 6a-prime entry among recorded ones has no warning of its own (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) no entry is written for a record with no `implementation_authors` field, a module with\n  no well-formed author entry, or a record holding a malformed one (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) the author-before-review ordering is prose, not refused by code (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) a history array added to the schema later and not added to `APPEND_ONLY` (FR-7);\n- (v1.2) rows moved by an edit wider than this design describes (Mutation rows, \"Existing rows\");\n- (v1.4) a class-(b) target ending in `/` that names no existing directory passes T2a and is\n  judged as a file name (FR-4, OD-2);\n- (v1.4) a self-check FAIL added later is classed by the verdict/could-not-run rule, not listed\n  (FR-4 `--self-check`).\n1510→\n## Measurements\n\nTwo behavioural premises carry committed probes under `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`,\neach with its invocation in its docstring and one reading at `200ffd52`:\n- `fr3_state_line_grammar.py` (P-1..P-5, §\"FR-3\"): `PROBE: PASS`;\n- `fr6_import_failure_pair.py` (the hand-built gate trees, §\"FR-6\"): `PROBE: PASS`.\n\nThe census figures below are one reading at `29ae3e7b` each. Their committed probes are owed to\nthe impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\"); the scratch scripts that produced them were deleted,\n1520→and the method is stated beside each figure so a probe can re-derive it.\n\n| Figure | Method | Reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| DO-1a line census | `git ls-files -z h-mad \\| xargs -0 grep -l 'TDD-STATE: active'`, and the plan's four-pattern variant | 6 files; 7 files |\n| M-3, rows over the contract | the plan's pattern over the `find` + `replace` of rows naming the two FR-3 files | 8 rows, 3 specs |\n| rows inside the regions FR-3 rewrites | the `find` offset inside `_read_state`, the authorship block, `_active_records` or `format_state_line` | 13 rows |\n| M-4 over the DO-5 set | the `find` start inside a moved name's `ast` span, for rows naming the Codex gate | 31 of 62 rows, 4 specs |\n| class inventory | the first `init` event's `tools` | 58 names: (a) 11, (b) 5, (c) 1, (d) 41 |\n| live records with FR-1 keys | a key scan over two state files | 0 of 61 records |\n1530→\n## Operator decisions\n\n- **OQ-A — where the shared policy lives (DO-5): decided, spec D-12.** `h_mad_target_identity.py`.\n  A **new** module breaks `test_codex_gate_judge_timeout_reason` unmodified (§\"FR-6\", committed\n  probe). The alternatives v1.0 listed (a new module plus an edited test tree; loading the Codex\n  gate file through `importlib`) are not taken.\n- **OQ-B — FR-8 after the merge (DO-6): decided, spec D-13.** The post-merge stage in §\"FR-8\",\n  with the feature recorded COMPLETE only after it, and this repository's `.agents/hooks.json`\n  committed only on a passed refusal. The override-flag alternative is not taken.\n1540→- **OD-E2 — a durable author record (FR-7): decided 2026-10-16, option (a), spec FR-1 D-15.** The\n  `implementation_authors` field (§\"FR-1\"), appended through `--append` at each accepted\n  implementation dispatch and read as the only source of a module's author set (§\"FR-7\"). Option\n  (b), amending AC-7.3's expected outcome to \"no entry\", is not taken.\n- **OD-2 — a class-(b) directory target: decided 2026-10-16 (operator), impl-plan Task 6.** An\n  existing-directory target is refused `kind=judge-error` under `S` and allowed under `inactive`,\n  as T2a (§\"FR-4\"). Residual: a trailing-`/` path naming no existing directory.\n- **Self-check exits: decided 2026-10-16 (orchestrator, impl-plan cycles 1–2).** A verdict FAIL\n  exits 0 and a could-not-run FAIL exits 2 (§\"FR-4\" `--self-check`); the Codex gate's\n  `FAIL shell-policy` is corrected in impl-plan Task 4.\n1550→\n## Owed by other documents\n\nSpec v1.7 (`c117a695`) settled the v1.0 items it owned: the `codex_status` description pair\n(FR-1), the agy version (FR-8 §\"Version\", `1.4.0` at `200ffd52`), D-12, D-13, D-14 and FR-7\n§\"Attribution\". Still owed:\n- **Plan.** v1.1's plan items (M-4's 31 rows, DO-2's log version, D-12/D-13) are landed in plan\n  v1.6 (`8e242d06`); v1.2 contradicts nothing in it. Plan stage 7's attribution fixture is spec\n  AC-7.3's first; the plan does not yet carry AC-7.3's other three or the E7 re-anchors (§\"Mutation\n  rows\", \"Existing rows the edits move\"), which the impl-plan's FR-5 and FR-7 Tasks must carry.\n1560→- **Spec v1.8 (`bd508fbf`)** adopted the deliberate differences (FR-4), the kind rule, S5 and E4.\n  It names only `judge-error`, `tool-not-admitted` and the judge's kind; the closed set it defers\n  to is §\"FR-4\" \"The deny kinds\" (five gate kinds plus the judge's).\n- **Spec v1.9 (D-15)** carries `implementation_authors`, AC-1.3 and the pre-field fixture, and\n  scopes FR-7's \"no entry\" rule to the three closed cases this design follows. This design adds\n  the `APPEND_ONLY` `--set` refusal over it and over `review_independence` (§\"FR-7\"), which\n  spec v1.9 FR-7 §\"Record\" does not state; the spec owes either that rule or a reason it is out\n  of scope.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.3).** The FR-1 Task carries AC-1.3's `implementation_authors` fixtures; the\n  FR-7 Task carries the two `APPEND_ONLY` fixtures and their mutation row, and AC-7.3's pre-field\n1570→  fixture beside its other four; the FR-10 Task\n  carries the SKILL.md author-append step at 5e GREEN acceptance and at each accepted fix\n  dispatch.\n- **Impl-plan, AC-7.3's surface.** Attribution is orchestrator prose; AC-7.3's five fixtures need\n  a code surface to drive, which spec v1.8 also files as an OPEN-DECISION. OD-E2 leaves this open:\n  it makes the fixtures' inputs durable, not executable.\n- **Spec (v1.4 items).** Lines recording OD-2 (T2a, with its residual); FR-2 naming\n  `step5:implementer_invalid` and `step5:implementer_unresolved`, or adopting them from the\n  impl-plan (§\"FR-2\" \"The caller's halts\"); FR-4/FR-5 self-check: a verdict FAIL exits 0.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.4 item).** The Codex gate's `FAIL parser` is a verdict FAIL that returns 2 like\n1580→  `FAIL shell-policy`; Task 4 corrects only the latter by name. Either Task 4 corrects both, or the\n  impl-plan states why `FAIL parser` stays.\n- **Impl-plan.** These become committed probes: the M-3/M-4 censuses, the class inventory, the FR-9\n  corpus reading and the replay. The FR-3 grammar probe and the FR-6 import-failure probe are\n  committed by this design. Each FR-9/FR-10 Task's RED names the doc-pin census entries it moves.\n\n## Version History\n- v1.0: Initial design (2026-10-16) from spec v1.6 (c853b207) and plan v1.4 (29ae3e7b), tree read at 29ae3e7b. Settles DO-1..DO-7: per-record author field on TDD-STATE (P-1..P-5 probed in Python re and bash 3.2/5.3 ERE); 11-name class-(a) allowlist over the 58-name init.tools inventory; locked --append writer operation; stdlib RFC 3339 predicate in classify on both validator paths, scoped to implementer_switch.ts; 25 moved names into h_mad_target_identity.py with guarded import (M-4 re-derived: 31 rows, 4 specs); HOME-fixture tests and post-merge FR-8 stage; prose-applied carve-out with six per-copy locators and 8 control rows. Two operator questions (OQ-A placement, OQ-B post-merge tracer); codex_status description owed to the spec.\n- v1.1: Design audit cycle 1 (2026-10-16), against spec v1.7 (c117a695), tree at 200ffd52. C1: leap second refused per spec FR-1/D-14, residual framing dropped. C2/C3: FR-4 class (b) is the Codex gate per-target sequence T1-T7 (unresolvable, containment before _is_shell_allowance, every hard-link name for production, read_chain unreadable/inactive branches, no rglob-inactive shortcut per M:G5, non-empty artifactDirectoryPath), deliberate differences listed, target differential test. C4/C11: AC-9.1 WIRED fixture and three-hash assertion. C5: in-place append row dropped as unbitable, replaced by loss and accumulation mutants. C6: FR-7 attribution from accepted implementation dispatches per spec FR-7 Attribution, per-module 6a-prime entries, unrecorded detail text no longer reads implementer_switch. C7: --append accumulates from the updated record; same-key --set/--append refused. C8: import failure re-raised inside _main_guarded so row G2 stays killed; self-check FAIL policy-import. C9: class (c) cwd computed like _command_cwd, chdir only to an existing command directory, no judge-error on a bad Cwd. C10: _semantic_ok never raises; new properties after fallback_agent. M1: committed probes fr3_state_line_grammar.py and fr6_import_failure_pair.py (both PROBE: PASS at 200ffd52). OQ-A/OQ-B recorded as spec D-12/D-13.\n- v1.2: Design audit cycle 2, final corrective revision after the round cap, not re-audited (2026-10-16); spec v1.8 (bd508fbf), plan v1.6 (8e242d06), tree at cff71b49. E1: step-5 workspacePaths cross-check and class (c) missing CommandLine gated on S (active|unknown); every FR-4 deny tabulated with its gating (16 rows). E5: class (b) targets are recognised values that are a non-empty str, '' never canonicalised. E6: closed kind set - judge-error, tool-not-admitted, target-outside-root, allowance-file-write, shell-not-admitted, plus the judge's KINDS passthrough at T7; 'as the Codex gate does' claim corrected (6 of 13 Codex _deny calls kindless). E3: T4 row re-fixtured on a non-str artifactDirectoryPath under inactive; the empty-string arm declared an equivalent mutant (step-3 chdir). E2/E4: authors = accepted 5e GREEN + accepted fix dispatches, never 5d RED; complete set kept in procedure, never rebuilt from entries; lost list -> no entry; OD-E2 (AC-7.3 multi-author recovery needs a durable FR-1 record) to the impl-plan. E7: re-anchor of assemble_tdd_agent w10a-grok-by-default; t1, wr3 and two heartbeat_beat rows kept by stated line forms; --check-anchors rule per Task. E8: property_valid guards dict via _semantic_ok. New rows for the S-gates, the target test, the three design kinds, the dict guard.\n1590→- v1.3: Operator decision OD-E2 option (a) (2026-10-16), aligned to spec v1.9 D-15; tree at 3ad735f7. FR-1: fifth property implementation_authors, array of {module (string, minLength 1), agent (codex|agy|grok|claude)}, both required, no extra keys, placed after review_independence; minLength confirmed in _MiniDraft7's supported set; zero-record reading for the fifth key (54 + 8 records, 0 carrying any of the five keys). FR-7: the author record appended through the existing --append at each accepted 5e GREEN and accepted fix dispatch, never 5d RED, before any review leg of that code runs; the author set and the latest author are read from the field only (v1.2's in-procedure list retired); no entry only for an absent field, a module with no well-formed entry, or a malformed field; the AC-7.3 multi-author recovered and pre-field fixtures derived from durable state. New: APPEND_ONLY --set refusal in merge_fields over review_independence and implementation_authors, with a per-key mutation row (owed to the spec). OD-E2 closed in Operator decisions; Test Plan gains AC-1.3; Residuals, Components, FR-10 and Owed updated. AC-7.3's code surface stays the impl-plan's open decision.\n- v1.4: Owed lines from Phase 5b impl-plan audit cycle 2, final corrective, not re-audited (2026-10-16); impl-plan v1.1 (fc92becf), tree at 84ec2133. Q1: OD-2 recorded as FR-4 T2a (existing-directory target -> judge-error under S, allow under inactive; before T3), deny table 17 rows, deliberate difference, mutation row, residual (trailing '/' naming no directory), Operator decisions. Q2: --self-check rule - a verdict FAIL exits 0, a could-not-run FAIL (policy-import) exits 2; the Codex gate's FAIL shell-policy corrected in impl-plan Task 4, FAIL parser owed. Q3: FR-2 caller halts step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded, step5:implementer_invalid, step5:implementer_unresolved adopted from the impl-plan. Owed: spec lines for all three; impl-plan FAIL parser.\n\nSource spec: # Spec — agy as a peer Phase-5 implementer (`agy-coder-fallback`)\n\n> **Slug note.** The slug predates brainstorm v1.1 and is kept because the state record carries it.\n> agy is a **peer implementer** with Codex's standing, not a fallback.\n\nSource: `docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback-brainstorm.md` v1.1 (operator-approved\n2026-10-16). Every \"currently\" claim below was read from the tree at `a8d9ba99`; the command that\n1600→read it is named beside it.\n\n## Problem\n\nCodex is the only Phase-5 implementer h-mad accepts. The seams that hard-code it are listed here:\n\n- **State.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` declares `codex_status` and `fallback_agent`\n  (`grok|claude|null`) and sets `\"additionalProperties\": false`. Any new key must therefore be\n  declared there, or `h_mad_state_write.py` rejects it. (Read with `cat` on the schema.)\n- **Claude-side authorship gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` refuses Claude's production write\n1610→  as `codex-authorship` when `HMAD_CODEX_UNAVAILABLE` is empty, the state line says\n  `codex-escape=no`, and `command -v codex` succeeds. Otherwise it folds `fallback_agent` into\n  `fallback-grok` / `fallback-invalid`. (`grep -n 'codex-authorship\\|fallback-grok' hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh`.)\n- **Single state source.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` `read_chain` collects every `step5`\n  record on the target's `docs/.bkit-memory.json` chain into `Record(key, codex_status, state_file,\n  fallback)`. `format_state_line` prints `TDD-STATE: active codex-escape=… blocker=… records=…\n  fallback=… record=…`, and the hook parses that line with `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`. The judge's\n  `ESCAPE_STATUSES` is `{\"unavailable\", \"exhausted\"}`.\n- **Staging.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` accepts `--agent` with `choices=(\"codex\",\n  \"grok\")`. The default timeout is 1500 for grok and 900 otherwise. `command_block` derives a\n1620→  non-codex first line from the codex line. The test\n  `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` pins that the prompt bytes do not depend on `--agent`.\n- **Prompt.** `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` opens \"You are Codex implementing…\"\n  and its `Hook:` line names only Codex's and Claude's gates. Because that test pins one prompt\n  for every agent, grok is told it is Codex today.\n- **Write gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` speaks Codex's hook contract. Its\n  `permissionDecision` deny goes out under `hookSpecificOutput`. agy's contract is\n  `{\"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": …}` on stdout (`h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` §\"Hooks\",\n  §\"The TDD gate\"). No agy gate exists, and that section prescribes the halt\n  `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` until one is verified against a real refusal.\n1630→\n## Terms\n\n- **Peer**: `codex` or `agy`. **Fallback**: `fallback_agent`, which is `grok`, `claude`, or\n  absent/`null` (equivalent to `claude`).\n- **Chosen implementer**: the record's `implementer` field. Absent or `null` reads as `codex`.\n- **Resolved implementer**: who actually authors Phase 5 for a record. FR-2 defines it.\n- **Active step5**: at least one record on the governing state chain has `phase == \"step5\"`. This\n  is the same predicate both existing gates use.\n\n1640→## Requirements\n\n### FR-1 — State fields\n\nAdd to `h_mad_state_schema.json`. Every field is OPTIONAL and additive, so `required` does not\nchange and records written before this feature stay valid:\n\n| field | values | absent means |\n|---|---|---|\n| `implementer` | `\"codex\"` \\| `\"agy\"` \\| `null` | `codex` |\n1650→| `agy_status` | `\"available\"` \\| `\"unavailable\"` \\| `\"exhausted\"` \\| `null` | `available` |\n| `implementer_switch` | object `{from, to, reason, ts}` \\| `null` | no switch has happened |\n| `review_independence` | array of objects `{leg, module, reviewer, implementer, independent}` | nothing recorded |\n| `implementation_authors` | array of objects `{module, agent}` (D-15) | no implementation dispatch recorded |\n"}}],"rawOutput":{"type":"ReadFile","FileContent":{"content":"1255→  `getattr(<mod>, \"<callee>\")` at the RED base.\n- **The missing-symbol role** comes from the fixture's declaration. The test asserts that the\n  exception line names that symbol.\n- **Two classifiers transcribe the two texts.**\n  - `old_rule`: a missing-symbol RED (`ImportError`, `ModuleNotFoundError`, `AttributeError` or\n1260→    `NameError`) is a halt.\n  - `new_rule`: such a RED is valid iff the missing symbol is the caller and the callee resolves.\n  - The test also asserts that `CANONICAL`, imported from the equivalence test, contains\n    `the missing symbol is the caller the task creates` and `the callee resolves at the RED base`.\n    That ties the transcription to the words.\n- **Pass:** the set of cases whose verdict changed equals `{new-caller}`.\n- **Control:** two rows in the same new spec, each run alone. One drops the callee condition, and\n  `both-missing` then changes. The other drops the caller condition, and `other-symbol` and\n  `unrelated-import` then change.\n- The cases' exception lines and verdicts are also written to\n1270→  `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/` as the committed reading.\n\n**The incident replay (AC-9.3).** It is a committed probe under\n`docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`, following FR-9's four steps through `git archive`\nexports, so the live clone is never checked out. The premises were re-checked at `29ae3e7b`:\nHemaSuite `HEAD` is `77fb16f51`, and `531a6296b`, `7aa0d9dec` and `c2d671f6b` are each ancestors\n(`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). Their subjects begin `…Task 4 FR-1 resolver`,\n`…Task 5 FR-5 initiali…` and `…Task 6 CLI surface…`. The probe stamps the HemaSuite sha it reads.\n\n### FR-10 — documentation surfaces\n1280→\nThese follow the spec's FR-10 list and the plan's doc-pin census. Each rewrite keeps every pinned\nliteral the census lists, or changes that test's literal in the same commit.\n- **SKILL.md §\"Codex authors Phase 5 — enforced, not just instructed\"** becomes implementer-neutral.\n  It states FR-2 and FR-3 and names `agy-authorship`, `implementer-invalid` and\n  `h_mad_tdd_judge.py implementer`. The heading and the end anchor\n  `Phase 5 implementation is **Codex's job**` stay, or `_phase_5e_text` and `PHASE5_HEADING` move\n  in the same commit.\n- **SKILL.md §\"Exit-code dispatch for 5d/5e\"** gains a line that holds both `exec agy` and\n  \"implement\", plus the `TDD-IMPLEMENTER:` staging step.\n1290→- **SKILL.md, Phase 7 closure item 7** carries every `WARNING` line, and adds the FR-7 `--append`\n  step after each leg, for every implementer.\n- **SKILL.md's 5e bullet, and each fix-dispatch step** (v1.3), gain the FR-7 author append at\n  acceptance, ordered before the leg that reviews the code; the 5d bullet gains none.\n- **The SKILL.md teammate-audit bullet** separates audit-leg selection from resolved authorship.\n- **SKILL.md** states the FR-5 re-run trigger: after any agy upgrade, re-run FR-8 step 2 and step\n  2a, and re-take the class-(a) inventory.\n- **`agy-runtime.md` §\"The TDD gate\"** names `h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` and `AGY-GATE:`, and keeps the\n  halt. Its `SessionStart` claim, on two surfaces, is re-checked against the installed agy, which\n  is `1.4.0` at `29ae3e7b`.\n1300→- **The prompt** gets a neutral opening and a `Hook:` line that names each gate by implementer,\n  with no `<`, `>` or `->`.\n- **`state-schema.md` and the schema** get the FR-1 rows, plus the four description rewrites in\n  §\"FR-1\".\n- **`failure-recovery.md`** gets copy 4.\n\n## Components Changed / Added\n\n| Path | Change | FR |\n|---|---|---|\n1310→| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` | five properties; `fallback_agent` and `codex_status` descriptions | FR-1 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_validate.py` | `rfc3339_datetime`, `_semantic_ok` in `classify`, `property_valid` | FR-1, FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` | `Record` fields, `_implementer_tag`, `Implementer`, `resolve_implementer`, author field, `implementer` verb | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` | `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`, author-field parse, FR-3 precedence | FR-3 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_target_identity.py` | receives the 25 moved names | FR-6 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` | guarded import of the 25 names; definitions removed | FR-6 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` (new) | agy write gate | FR-4 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_hook_wiring.py` | `--agy`, `check_agy` | FR-5 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` | `agy` choice, timeout table, check run, docstring, copy 5 | FR-5, FR-8, FR-9 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_write.py` | `--append`; the `APPEND_ONLY` refusal in `merge_fields` | FR-7 |\n1320→| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` | `_review_independence_warnings` | FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` | neutral opening, `Hook:` line, copies 1, 2 and 6 | FR-9 |\n| `h-mad/SKILL.md`, `h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md`, `h-mad/references/state-schema.md`, `h-mad/references/failure-recovery.md` | §\"FR-10\" | FR-9, FR-10 |\n| `.agents/hooks.json` (new, committed by FR-8's stage) | wiring | FR-5, D-2 |\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. FR-1: the schema, the validator predicate and `property_valid`.\n2. FR-2: the resolver and the verb.\n3. FR-3: the line, the hook, the stub re-shape, `ACTIVE_RE`, and the re-anchoring of every row of\n1330→   the two files.\n4. FR-6: the move, the guarded import, the 31 re-pointed rows, and the identity module's anchor\n   recheck.\n5. FR-4, then FR-5.\n6. FR-7: `--append`, then the warnings.\n7. FR-9 and FR-10: the copies, the equivalence test, the corpus, the doc rewrites, then the replay\n   probe.\n8. Merge, then FR-8's stage (OQ-B, spec D-13).\n\nEach Task runs the full h-mad suite, under `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python3`, in the foreground, and\n1340→gates on the summary line.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n| AC | Where |\n|---|---|\n| AC-1.1 | `test_h_mad_state_validate_fallback.py` gains each FR-1 field × value × path (`implementation_authors`'s fixtures are AC-1.3's); `test_h_mad_state_fallback_agent.py` stays green |\n| AC-1.2 | new fixtures beside it: the 5 refused values, the 2 accepted values and the zone-branch fixtures, × 2 paths |\n| AC-1.3 | `test_h_mad_state_validate_fallback.py`, each fixture once per path through `_FORCE_FALLBACK`, as spec v1.9 AC-1.3 lists them: accepted `[]`, one entry per agent (four fixtures), and the three-entry `[m/agy, m/codex, m/agy]` log (duplicates and order kept); refused, each its own fixture, an unknown agent, a missing `agent`, a missing `module`, `\"module\":\"\"`, an extra key, a non-object entry and a non-array value; a record with no `implementation_authors` unchanged; and a refused `--append implementation_authors=…` leaving the store byte-identical (`test_h_mad_state_write.py`) |\n| AC-2.1, AC-2.2 | `test_h_mad_tdd_judge.py`, with `env` and `which` injected; the verb through `_cli` |\n1350→| AC-3.1, AC-3.2 | `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_judge.py` and `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_fallback_agent.py` (re-shaped literals only); new kinds in a new `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_peers.py`; a `bin_dir` with an `agy` stub drives `agy-authorship` |\n| AC-4.1, AC-4.2 | new `test_h_mad_agy_tdd_gate.py`, including the **target differential**: a corpus of target shapes (in-root production `.py`; a test file; `src/test_a.py` hard-linked to `src/z.py`; the allowance file in two case spellings; `docs/x.py`; `/tmp` non-`.py`; `/tmp` `.py`; an outside non-`/tmp` path; an unresolvable path; a production `.py` whose chain holds a `chmod 000` `docs/` that the `rglob` scan cannot see) × `phase5_status` (`active`, `inactive`, `unknown`), each judged by the Codex gate (`Write` with `file_path`, no payload cwd) and by the agy gate (`write_to_file` with `TargetFile`), with the same admit/deny in every cell outside the stated deliberate differences, and the same kind wherever the Codex deny carries one; plus the class-(c) workdir fixtures and the shell differential (§\"FR-4\"); plus, under `inactive`, `run_command` `ls` with `workspacePaths=[]`, `run_command` with no `CommandLine`, and `write_to_file` with `TargetFile: \"\"` each allowed, and the same three under `active` and under `unknown` each denied `kind=judge-error`; plus one fixture per row of §\"FR-4\" \"Every deny\" asserting that row's kind, and a scan of every deny the suite produces asserting exactly one `kind=` token from the closed set |\n| AC-5.1, AC-5.2 | new `test_h_mad_hook_wiring_agy.py` (a `HOME` fixture), plus `test_h_mad_assemble_tdd_agent.py` |\n| AC-6.1 | the existing Codex gate tests unmodified (`test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]` is the import-failure fixture); the new `--self-check` `FAIL policy-import` fixture; the one-`def` test; the `unsafe` tuple parity test; the shell differential |\n| AC-7.1, AC-7.2 | `test_h_mad_state_write.py` (`--append`: the two-entry fixture, the two-appends-in-one-call fixture, the same-key `--set`/`--append` refusal, and the `APPEND_ONLY` refusal once per key with that key alone: `--set review_independence=[]` and `--set implementation_authors=[]`, each exit 2 with the store unchanged) and `test_h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py`; the FR-7 attribution rule is orchestrator prose (SKILL.md, FR-10), pinned by a doc test that the FR-7 step's text states the dispatch as the source; the one code surface that names an author, the `unrecorded` detail text, gets the switch/recovery fixture: `implementer_switch.to == \"agy\"` with a well-formed 5e entry whose `implementer` is `codex`, and the detail must name `codex` and not `agy`; `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)` is `True` and does not raise. AC-7.3's attribution fixtures (spec v1.9: the four of v1.8 plus the pre-field fixture) are each derivable from the record alone, the multi-author recovered one included, since the author set is read from `implementation_authors` (§\"FR-7\", OD-E2 decided); they still have no code surface to drive, since attribution is orchestrator prose, and that surface is owed to the impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\") |\n| AC-8.1, AC-8.2 | probes, §\"FR-8\" |\n| AC-9.1 | `test_h_mad_assemble_tdd_agent.py` `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` is extended: the WIRED fixture (§\"FR-5\") is provisioned in its `tmp_path` root once, before the loop, so all three agents read the same root; the loop becomes `(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\")`; `run_cli` gains an env override so the `agy` run sees the fixture `HOME`; and the assertion becomes `len(hashes) == 3 and len(set(hashes)) == 1`. Today it loops over `(\"codex\", \"grok\")` and asserts `hashes[0] == hashes[1]`, which would leave a third hash unchecked. Plus the union sweep re-run and the three pin files staying green |\n| AC-9.2, AC-9.4 | §\"FR-9\" |\n| AC-9.3 | probe |\n| AC-X | §\"Mutation rows\" |\n1360→\n## Mutation rows (AC-X)\n\nEach new guard below gets one row. The fixture that kills it is named beside it.\n- **FR-1**\n  - `_semantic_ok` call removed from `classify` → `not-a-date` on both paths.\n  - The `datetime` construction removed → `2026-02-30T00:00:00Z`.\n  - `fullmatch` → `match` → `…Zjunk`.\n- **FR-2**\n  - Each `_cause` branch removed → that branch's own fixture, with only that cause present.\n1370→  - The `other` peer step removed → `chosen=codex` out, agy available.\n- **FR-3**\n  - The `implementer-invalid` branch removed → the invalid fixture.\n  - The `INVALID_RECORD` scan stopped at the first record → `[codex-available, invalid]` expects\n    `implementer-invalid`.\n  - The `agy` arm removed → the `agy-authorship` fixture.\n  - The grammar's `peers-out` alternative removed → every stub test.\n- **FR-6**\n  - The import guard removed (a bare top-level import) → `test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]`,\n    whose tree has no identity module: the gate then exits 1 with no JSON.\n1380→  - The self-check's `FAIL policy-import` branch removed → the new self-check fixture, which then\n    sees a `NameError` traceback and exit 1.\n  - Row `G2` itself stays killed through the re-raise (§\"FR-6\", Binding).\n  - No row for removing the `_main_guarded` re-raise, because that mutant is equivalent in\n    decision: without it, every path of `_main_guarded` that can allow first calls a moved name\n    (`_any_phase5_status` runs before any allow), which raises `NameError` into `# M:G2` and\n    denies `judge-error`; the one earlier deny (`M:CX-ROOT-ENTER`) is a deny either way. Only the\n    reason text differs. The re-raise exists so the reason names the import failure.\n- **FR-4**\n  - A class-(a) name moved to (b) or (d) → that class's member fixture.\n1390→  - The class-(d) default replaced by allow → an unknown-name fixture.\n  - The no-path-key deny removed → that fixture.\n  - The `artifactDirectoryPath` `.py` refusal removed → its fixture.\n  - The `finally` deny removed → malformed stdin.\n  - T3 moved after T5 (allowance check before containment) → a `/tmp` non-`.py` write, which then\n    denies `judge-error` instead of allowing.\n  - (v1.4) T2a removed → a `write_to_file` whose `TargetFile` names an existing in-root directory\n    under `active`, which then allows instead of denying `judge-error` (the impl-plan's\n    `od2-directory-target-check-dropped`).\n  - T6 judging `resolved.target` alone instead of every name → the `test_a.py`/`z.py` hard-link\n1400→    fixture.\n  - T6–T7 skipped when `phase5_status == \"inactive\"` → the `chmod 000` `docs/` chain fixture.\n  - T7's `unreadable` branch removed → the same fixture.\n  - T4's `str` check on `artifactDirectoryPath` (`isinstance(adp, str) and adp` → `adp is not\n    None`) → `artifactDirectoryPath: 5` with a non-`.py` target outside both `/tmp` and the root,\n    under `inactive`: the rule allows; the mutant reaches `Path(5)`, raises `TypeError`, and denies\n    `kind=judge-error`. v1.1's fixture (`\"\"`, from a process directory containing the target)\n    could not bite: step 3's `os.chdir(root)` makes `Path(\"\")` the root, and T3 has already sent\n    every in-root target away, so `\"\"` admits nothing either way (design audit cycle 2, codex,\n    run on `_path_within` as a controlled pair). **The empty-string arm is therefore an\n1410→    equivalent mutant at the full gate** and has no row; it stays as defence should step 3's\n    `chdir` move. Residual: that arm is unpinned.\n  - Step 5's `S` condition removed → `run_command` `ls`, `workspacePaths=[]`, `inactive`, which\n    then denies.\n  - Class (c)'s missing-`CommandLine` `S` condition removed → `run_command` with no `CommandLine`,\n    `inactive`, which then denies.\n  - Class (b)'s non-empty-`str` target test weakened to key presence → `TargetFile: \"\"` under\n    `active`, which then allows (no production name) instead of denying `kind=judge-error`.\n  - Each of the three design-owned kinds replaced by `judge-error` at its site\n    (`target-outside-root`, `allowance-file-write`, `shell-not-admitted`) → that row's kind\n1420→    fixture.\n  - Class (c) denying `judge-error` when `cwd` is not an existing directory → `ls` with\n    `Cwd=str(root / \"no-such-dir\")`.\n  - Class (c) joining a relative `Cwd` against the handler's directory → a relative `Cwd` naming\n    a sub-project whose `.venv` interpreter the command uses.\n- **FR-5:** each of the seven reason checks removed → its fixture; `UNWIRED` returning 2 → the\n  AC-5.2 exit fixture.\n- **FR-7**\n  - Each appended value built from `[]` instead of the current value → AC-7.1's two-entry\n    fixture (both earlier entries, compared as `json.dumps` text, must survive).\n1430→  - Accumulation read from `prior` instead of the updated `record` → the two-appends-in-one-call\n    fixture (both earlier entries and both additions, in order).\n  - The same-key `--set`/`--append` refusal removed → its fixture, which expects exit 2 and an\n    unchanged store.\n  - (v1.3) Each `APPEND_ONLY` member removed from the tuple → that key's own `--set …=[]` fixture,\n    run with that key alone, which expects exit 2 and an unchanged store.\n  - v1.0's row \"`--append` mutating the prior list in place\" is dropped: the prior record is\n    discarded after the write, so the persisted bytes are identical in both modes and no\n    observation the suite makes can see it (codex audit cycle 1, run on a controlled pair).\n  - The `independent` consistency check removed → a lying-boolean fixture.\n1440→  - The `unrecorded` trigger restricted to `implementer == \"agy\"` → the `codex` fixture (AC-7.2).\n  - A malformed 6a-prime entry counted as recorded → its fixture.\n  - The `unrecorded` detail text reading `implementer_switch.to` → the switch/recovery fixture.\n  - `property_valid`'s `dict` guard removed (the predicate applied to `value[\"ts\"]` directly) →\n    `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)`, which then raises.\n- **FR-9:** the 8 + 2 rows in §\"FR-9\".\n\n**Existing rows the edits move (E7).** The rule over the class: after each Task, every committed\nmutation row whose `file` the Task edits must still match its `find` exactly once\n(`h_mad_mutation_harness.py --check-anchors`, the harness's own `source.count(find)` test), and a\n1450→row the edit breaks is re-anchored **in that Task**, to the same intent and the same `test`. The\nsweep that found them: every row of `h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/*.json` whose `file` is one this\ndesign edits outside FR-3's and FR-6's files (which §\"FR-3\" and §\"FR-6\" already re-anchor\nwhole), with each `find` located in the file at `cff71b49`:\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `w10a-grok-by-default` (FR-5 Task): its `find` is the `--agent`\n  choices line, which FR-5 rewrites. Re-anchor: `find`\n  `ap.add_argument(\"--agent\", choices=(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\"), default=\"codex\")`, `replace` the\n  same with `default=\"grok\"`, `test` unchanged.\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `t1-timeout-judged-by-value` (FR-5 Task): `find`\n  `args.timeout is not None` sits on the timeout line FR-5 rewrites; the line form in §\"FR-5\"\n1460→  keeps it once, and the `replace` (`args.timeout not in (None, 900)`) still bites\n  `test_agent_grok_explicit_timeout_wins`. No re-anchor if that form is kept.\n- `grok_wire_reverts.json` `wr3-assembler-drops-agent` (FR-5 Task): `find` `        agent=args.agent,`\n  must stay once; the check run FR-5 adds to `main` must not repeat that line.\n- `heartbeat_beat.json` `the-owners-set-no-longer-beats` and `a-bystanders-set-beats-too` (FR-7\n  Task): `find` is `merge_fields`' owner-heartbeat `if` and its assignment; §\"FR-7\" keeps both\n  byte for byte, so no re-anchor. The other two rows of that spec anchor in `beat`, which FR-7\n  does not edit.\n- SKILL.md and `failure-recovery.md` rows: none of their `find` texts lies in a span FR-9/FR-10\n  rewrites (the nearest are `phase7_integrate_blockers_documented.json`'s three rows inside Phase 7\n1470→  item 7 (the closure list, around its 7f integrate step), which the item-7 edit only adds to, and\n  `baseline_sha.json`/`wire_registry_key.json` in §\"Phase 5 (Implementation) sub-steps\" on the 5f\n  bullet, not the 5d bullet FR-9 edits). Every other row on\n  `h_mad_assemble_tdd.py`, `h_mad_state_write.py`, `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` and\n  `h_mad_hook_wiring.py` anchors on code this design does not rewrite. `h_mad_state_validate.py`,\n  `h_mad_state_schema.json` and `codex-implementer-prompt.md` have no rows.\nResidual: the sweep reads the design's edit sites as described here; an implementation that\nrewrites more than it describes moves rows this list does not name, which `--check-anchors` then\ncatches in that Task.\n\n1480→## Residuals\n\nEach is stated where it arises. Collected here:\n- the `which` / `command -v` matrix (FR-2);\n- the verb reads the root only (FR-2);\n- the class-(a) judgement (FR-4);\n- the six-line shell composition in both gates (FR-4);\n- a sibling `overwrite` (FR-4);\n- the review-leg agy is gated too (FR-4);\n- worktree state, not claimed either way (FR-4);\n1490→- an equivalent command spelling (FR-5);\n- a writer that bypasses `_mutate` (FR-7);\n- the deliberate differences from the Codex gate's target sequence, and any rule it gains later\n  (FR-4);\n- relative shell tokens under a `Cwd` that does not exist (FR-4);\n- code a reviewer wrote outside an implementation dispatch (FR-7);\n- prose application (FR-9);\n- a contradicting sentence or a seventh surface (FR-9);\n- (v1.2) a judge kind added to `KINDS` later passes through unlisted (FR-4);\n- (v1.2) T4's empty-string arm is an equivalent mutant, unpinned (Mutation rows);\n1500→- (v1.2) a module missing its 6a-prime entry among recorded ones has no warning of its own (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) no entry is written for a record with no `implementation_authors` field, a module with\n  no well-formed author entry, or a record holding a malformed one (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) the author-before-review ordering is prose, not refused by code (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) a history array added to the schema later and not added to `APPEND_ONLY` (FR-7);\n- (v1.2) rows moved by an edit wider than this design describes (Mutation rows, \"Existing rows\");\n- (v1.4) a class-(b) target ending in `/` that names no existing directory passes T2a and is\n  judged as a file name (FR-4, OD-2);\n- (v1.4) a self-check FAIL added later is classed by the verdict/could-not-run rule, not listed\n  (FR-4 `--self-check`).\n1510→\n## Measurements\n\nTwo behavioural premises carry committed probes under `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`,\neach with its invocation in its docstring and one reading at `200ffd52`:\n- `fr3_state_line_grammar.py` (P-1..P-5, §\"FR-3\"): `PROBE: PASS`;\n- `fr6_import_failure_pair.py` (the hand-built gate trees, §\"FR-6\"): `PROBE: PASS`.\n\nThe census figures below are one reading at `29ae3e7b` each. Their committed probes are owed to\nthe impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\"); the scratch scripts that produced them were deleted,\n1520→and the method is stated beside each figure so a probe can re-derive it.\n\n| Figure | Method | Reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| DO-1a line census | `git ls-files -z h-mad \\| xargs -0 grep -l 'TDD-STATE: active'`, and the plan's four-pattern variant | 6 files; 7 files |\n| M-3, rows over the contract | the plan's pattern over the `find` + `replace` of rows naming the two FR-3 files | 8 rows, 3 specs |\n| rows inside the regions FR-3 rewrites | the `find` offset inside `_read_state`, the authorship block, `_active_records` or `format_state_line` | 13 rows |\n| M-4 over the DO-5 set | the `find` start inside a moved name's `ast` span, for rows naming the Codex gate | 31 of 62 rows, 4 specs |\n| class inventory | the first `init` event's `tools` | 58 names: (a) 11, (b) 5, (c) 1, (d) 41 |\n| live records with FR-1 keys | a key scan over two state files | 0 of 61 records |\n1530→\n## Operator decisions\n\n- **OQ-A — where the shared policy lives (DO-5): decided, spec D-12.** `h_mad_target_identity.py`.\n  A **new** module breaks `test_codex_gate_judge_timeout_reason` unmodified (§\"FR-6\", committed\n  probe). The alternatives v1.0 listed (a new module plus an edited test tree; loading the Codex\n  gate file through `importlib`) are not taken.\n- **OQ-B — FR-8 after the merge (DO-6): decided, spec D-13.** The post-merge stage in §\"FR-8\",\n  with the feature recorded COMPLETE only after it, and this repository's `.agents/hooks.json`\n  committed only on a passed refusal. The override-flag alternative is not taken.\n1540→- **OD-E2 — a durable author record (FR-7): decided 2026-10-16, option (a), spec FR-1 D-15.** The\n  `implementation_authors` field (§\"FR-1\"), appended through `--append` at each accepted\n  implementation dispatch and read as the only source of a module's author set (§\"FR-7\"). Option\n  (b), amending AC-7.3's expected outcome to \"no entry\", is not taken.\n- **OD-2 — a class-(b) directory target: decided 2026-10-16 (operator), impl-plan Task 6.** An\n  existing-directory target is refused `kind=judge-error` under `S` and allowed under `inactive`,\n  as T2a (§\"FR-4\"). Residual: a trailing-`/` path naming no existing directory.\n- **Self-check exits: decided 2026-10-16 (orchestrator, impl-plan cycles 1–2).** A verdict FAIL\n  exits 0 and a could-not-run FAIL exits 2 (§\"FR-4\" `--self-check`); the Codex gate's\n  `FAIL shell-policy` is corrected in impl-plan Task 4.\n1550→\n## Owed by other documents\n\nSpec v1.7 (`c117a695`) settled the v1.0 items it owned: the `codex_status` description pair\n(FR-1), the agy version (FR-8 §\"Version\", `1.4.0` at `200ffd52`), D-12, D-13, D-14 and FR-7\n§\"Attribution\". Still owed:\n- **Plan.** v1.1's plan items (M-4's 31 rows, DO-2's log version, D-12/D-13) are landed in plan\n  v1.6 (`8e242d06`); v1.2 contradicts nothing in it. Plan stage 7's attribution fixture is spec\n  AC-7.3's first; the plan does not yet carry AC-7.3's other three or the E7 re-anchors (§\"Mutation\n  rows\", \"Existing rows the edits move\"), which the impl-plan's FR-5 and FR-7 Tasks must carry.\n1560→- **Spec v1.8 (`bd508fbf`)** adopted the deliberate differences (FR-4), the kind rule, S5 and E4.\n  It names only `judge-error`, `tool-not-admitted` and the judge's kind; the closed set it defers\n  to is §\"FR-4\" \"The deny kinds\" (five gate kinds plus the judge's).\n- **Spec v1.9 (D-15)** carries `implementation_authors`, AC-1.3 and the pre-field fixture, and\n  scopes FR-7's \"no entry\" rule to the three closed cases this design follows. This design adds\n  the `APPEND_ONLY` `--set` refusal over it and over `review_independence` (§\"FR-7\"), which\n  spec v1.9 FR-7 §\"Record\" does not state; the spec owes either that rule or a reason it is out\n  of scope.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.3).** The FR-1 Task carries AC-1.3's `implementation_authors` fixtures; the\n  FR-7 Task carries the two `APPEND_ONLY` fixtures and their mutation row, and AC-7.3's pre-field\n1570→  fixture beside its other four; the FR-10 Task\n  carries the SKILL.md author-append step at 5e GREEN acceptance and at each accepted fix\n  dispatch.\n- **Impl-plan, AC-7.3's surface.** Attribution is orchestrator prose; AC-7.3's five fixtures need\n  a code surface to drive, which spec v1.8 also files as an OPEN-DECISION. OD-E2 leaves this open:\n  it makes the fixtures' inputs durable, not executable.\n- **Spec (v1.4 items).** Lines recording OD-2 (T2a, with its residual); FR-2 naming\n  `step5:implementer_invalid` and `step5:implementer_unresolved`, or adopting them from the\n  impl-plan (§\"FR-2\" \"The caller's halts\"); FR-4/FR-5 self-check: a verdict FAIL exits 0.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.4 item).** The Codex gate's `FAIL parser` is a verdict FAIL that returns 2 like\n1580→  `FAIL shell-policy`; Task 4 corrects only the latter by name. Either Task 4 corrects both, or the\n  impl-plan states why `FAIL parser` stays.\n- **Impl-plan.** These become committed probes: the M-3/M-4 censuses, the class inventory, the FR-9\n  corpus reading and the replay. The FR-3 grammar probe and the FR-6 import-failure probe are\n  committed by this design. Each FR-9/FR-10 Task's RED names the doc-pin census entries it moves.\n\n## Version History\n- v1.0: Initial design (2026-10-16) from spec v1.6 (c853b207) and plan v1.4 (29ae3e7b), tree read at 29ae3e7b. Settles DO-1..DO-7: per-record author field on TDD-STATE (P-1..P-5 probed in Python re and bash 3.2/5.3 ERE); 11-name class-(a) allowlist over the 58-name init.tools inventory; locked --append writer operation; stdlib RFC 3339 predicate in classify on both validator paths, scoped to implementer_switch.ts; 25 moved names into h_mad_target_identity.py with guarded import (M-4 re-derived: 31 rows, 4 specs); HOME-fixture tests and post-merge FR-8 stage; prose-applied carve-out with six per-copy locators and 8 control rows. Two operator questions (OQ-A placement, OQ-B post-merge tracer); codex_status description owed to the spec.\n- v1.1: Design audit cycle 1 (2026-10-16), against spec v1.7 (c117a695), tree at 200ffd52. C1: leap second refused per spec FR-1/D-14, residual framing dropped. C2/C3: FR-4 class (b) is the Codex gate per-target sequence T1-T7 (unresolvable, containment before _is_shell_allowance, every hard-link name for production, read_chain unreadable/inactive branches, no rglob-inactive shortcut per M:G5, non-empty artifactDirectoryPath), deliberate differences listed, target differential test. C4/C11: AC-9.1 WIRED fixture and three-hash assertion. C5: in-place append row dropped as unbitable, replaced by loss and accumulation mutants. C6: FR-7 attribution from accepted implementation dispatches per spec FR-7 Attribution, per-module 6a-prime entries, unrecorded detail text no longer reads implementer_switch. C7: --append accumulates from the updated record; same-key --set/--append refused. C8: import failure re-raised inside _main_guarded so row G2 stays killed; self-check FAIL policy-import. C9: class (c) cwd computed like _command_cwd, chdir only to an existing command directory, no judge-error on a bad Cwd. C10: _semantic_ok never raises; new properties after fallback_agent. M1: committed probes fr3_state_line_grammar.py and fr6_import_failure_pair.py (both PROBE: PASS at 200ffd52). OQ-A/OQ-B recorded as spec D-12/D-13.\n- v1.2: Design audit cycle 2, final corrective revision after the round cap, not re-audited (2026-10-16); spec v1.8 (bd508fbf), plan v1.6 (8e242d06), tree at cff71b49. E1: step-5 workspacePaths cross-check and class (c) missing CommandLine gated on S (active|unknown); every FR-4 deny tabulated with its gating (16 rows). E5: class (b) targets are recognised values that are a non-empty str, '' never canonicalised. E6: closed kind set - judge-error, tool-not-admitted, target-outside-root, allowance-file-write, shell-not-admitted, plus the judge's KINDS passthrough at T7; 'as the Codex gate does' claim corrected (6 of 13 Codex _deny calls kindless). E3: T4 row re-fixtured on a non-str artifactDirectoryPath under inactive; the empty-string arm declared an equivalent mutant (step-3 chdir). E2/E4: authors = accepted 5e GREEN + accepted fix dispatches, never 5d RED; complete set kept in procedure, never rebuilt from entries; lost list -> no entry; OD-E2 (AC-7.3 multi-author recovery needs a durable FR-1 record) to the impl-plan. E7: re-anchor of assemble_tdd_agent w10a-grok-by-default; t1, wr3 and two heartbeat_beat rows kept by stated line forms; --check-anchors rule per Task. E8: property_valid guards dict via _semantic_ok. New rows for the S-gates, the target test, the three design kinds, the dict guard.\n1590→- v1.3: Operator decision OD-E2 option (a) (2026-10-16), aligned to spec v1.9 D-15; tree at 3ad735f7. FR-1: fifth property implementation_authors, array of {module (string, minLength 1), agent (codex|agy|grok|claude)}, both required, no extra keys, placed after review_independence; minLength confirmed in _MiniDraft7's supported set; zero-record reading for the fifth key (54 + 8 records, 0 carrying any of the five keys). FR-7: the author record appended through the existing --append at each accepted 5e GREEN and accepted fix dispatch, never 5d RED, before any review leg of that code runs; the author set and the latest author are read from the field only (v1.2's in-procedure list retired); no entry only for an absent field, a module with no well-formed entry, or a malformed field; the AC-7.3 multi-author recovered and pre-field fixtures derived from durable state. New: APPEND_ONLY --set refusal in merge_fields over review_independence and implementation_authors, with a per-key mutation row (owed to the spec). OD-E2 closed in Operator decisions; Test Plan gains AC-1.3; Residuals, Components, FR-10 and Owed updated. AC-7.3's code surface stays the impl-plan's open decision.\n- v1.4: Owed lines from Phase 5b impl-plan audit cycle 2, final corrective, not re-audited (2026-10-16); impl-plan v1.1 (fc92becf), tree at 84ec2133. Q1: OD-2 recorded as FR-4 T2a (existing-directory target -> judge-error under S, allow under inactive; before T3), deny table 17 rows, deliberate difference, mutation row, residual (trailing '/' naming no directory), Operator decisions. Q2: --self-check rule - a verdict FAIL exits 0, a could-not-run FAIL (policy-import) exits 2; the Codex gate's FAIL shell-policy corrected in impl-plan Task 4, FAIL parser owed. Q3: FR-2 caller halts step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded, step5:implementer_invalid, step5:implementer_unresolved adopted from the impl-plan. Owed: spec lines for all three; impl-plan FAIL parser.\n\nSource spec: # Spec — agy as a peer Phase-5 implementer (`agy-coder-fallback`)\n\n> **Slug note.** The slug predates brainstorm v1.1 and is kept because the state record carries it.\n> agy is a **peer implementer** with Codex's standing, not a fallback.\n\nSource: `docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback-brainstorm.md` v1.1 (operator-approved\n2026-10-16). Every \"currently\" claim below was read from the tree at `a8d9ba99`; the command that\n1600→read it is named beside it.\n\n## Problem\n\nCodex is the only Phase-5 implementer h-mad accepts. The seams that hard-code it are listed here:\n\n- **State.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` declares `codex_status` and `fallback_agent`\n  (`grok|claude|null`) and sets `\"additionalProperties\": false`. Any new key must therefore be\n  declared there, or `h_mad_state_write.py` rejects it. (Read with `cat` on the schema.)\n- **Claude-side authorship gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` refuses Claude's production write\n1610→  as `codex-authorship` when `HMAD_CODEX_UNAVAILABLE` is empty, the state line says\n  `codex-escape=no`, and `command -v codex` succeeds. Otherwise it folds `fallback_agent` into\n  `fallback-grok` / `fallback-invalid`. (`grep -n 'codex-authorship\\|fallback-grok' hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh`.)\n- **Single state source.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` `read_chain` collects every `step5`\n  record on the target's `docs/.bkit-memory.json` chain into `Record(key, codex_status, state_file,\n  fallback)`. `format_state_line` prints `TDD-STATE: active codex-escape=… blocker=… records=…\n  fallback=… record=…`, and the hook parses that line with `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`. The judge's\n  `ESCAPE_STATUSES` is `{\"unavailable\", \"exhausted\"}`.\n- **Staging.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` accepts `--agent` with `choices=(\"codex\",\n  \"grok\")`. The default timeout is 1500 for grok and 900 otherwise. `command_block` derives a\n1620→  non-codex first line from the codex line. The test\n  `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` pins that the prompt bytes do not depend on `--agent`.\n- **Prompt.** `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` opens \"You are Codex implementing…\"\n  and its `Hook:` line names only Codex's and Claude's gates. Because that test pins one prompt\n  for every agent, grok is told it is Codex today.\n- **Write gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` speaks Codex's hook contract. Its\n  `permissionDecision` deny goes out under `hookSpecificOutput`. agy's contract is\n  `{\"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": …}` on stdout (`h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` §\"Hooks\",\n  §\"The TDD gate\"). No agy gate exists, and that section prescribes the halt\n  `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` until one is verified against a real refusal.\n1630→\n## Terms\n\n- **Peer**: `codex` or `agy`. **Fallback**: `fallback_agent`, which is `grok`, `claude`, or\n  absent/`null` (equivalent to `claude`).\n- **Chosen implementer**: the record's `implementer` field. Absent or `null` reads as `codex`.\n- **Resolved implementer**: who actually authors Phase 5 for a record. FR-2 defines it.\n- **Active step5**: at least one record on the governing state chain has `phase == \"step5\"`. This\n  is the same predicate both existing gates use.\n\n1640→## Requirements\n\n### FR-1 — State fields\n\nAdd to `h_mad_state_schema.json`. Every field is OPTIONAL and additive, so `required` does not\nchange and records written before this feature stay valid:\n\n| field | values | absent means |\n|---|---|---|\n| `implementer` | `\"codex\"` \\| `\"agy\"` \\| `null` | `codex` |\n1650→| `agy_status` | `\"available\"` \\| `\"unavailable\"` \\| `\"exhausted\"` \\| `null` | `available` |\n| `implementer_switch` | object `{from, to, reason, ts}` \\| `null` | no switch has happened |\n| `review_independence` | array of objects `{leg, module, reviewer, implementer, independent}` | nothing recorded |\n| `implementation_authors` | array of objects `{module, agent}` (D-15) | no implementation dispatch recorded |\n","content_concise":"1255→  `getattr(<mod>, \"<callee>\")` at the RED base.\n- **The missing-symbol role** comes from the fixture's declaration. The test asserts that the\n  exception line names that symbol.\n- **Two classifiers transcribe the two texts.**\n  - `old_rule`: a missing-symbol RED (`ImportError`, `ModuleNotFoundError`, `AttributeError` or\n1260→    `NameError`) is a halt.\n  - `new_rule`: such a RED is valid iff the missing symbol is the caller and the callee resolves.\n  - The test also asserts that `CANONICAL`, imported from the equivalence test, contains\n    `the missing symbol is the caller the task creates` and `the callee resolves at the RED base`.\n    That ties the transcription to the words.\n- **Pass:** the set of cases whose verdict changed equals `{new-caller}`.\n- **Control:** two rows in the same new spec, each run alone. One drops the callee condition, and\n  `both-missing` then changes. The other drops the caller condition, and `other-symbol` and\n  `unrelated-import` then change.\n- The cases' exception lines and verdicts are also written to\n1270→  `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/` as the committed reading.\n\n**The incident replay (AC-9.3).** It is a committed probe under\n`docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`, following FR-9's four steps through `git archive`\nexports, so the live clone is never checked out. The premises were re-checked at `29ae3e7b`:\nHemaSuite `HEAD` is `77fb16f51`, and `531a6296b`, `7aa0d9dec` and `c2d671f6b` are each ancestors\n(`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). Their subjects begin `…Task 4 FR-1 resolver`,\n`…Task 5 FR-5 initiali…` and `…Task 6 CLI surface…`. The probe stamps the HemaSuite sha it reads.\n\n### FR-10 — documentation surfaces\n1280→\nThese follow the spec's FR-10 list and the plan's doc-pin census. Each rewrite keeps every pinned\nliteral the census lists, or changes that test's literal in the same commit.\n- **SKILL.md §\"Codex authors Phase 5 — enforced, not just instructed\"** becomes implementer-neutral.\n  It states FR-2 and FR-3 and names `agy-authorship`, `implementer-invalid` and\n  `h_mad_tdd_judge.py implementer`. The heading and the end anchor\n  `Phase 5 implementation is **Codex's job**` stay, or `_phase_5e_text` and `PHASE5_HEADING` move\n  in the same commit.\n- **SKILL.md §\"Exit-code dispatch for 5d/5e\"** gains a line that holds both `exec agy` and\n  \"implement\", plus the `TDD-IMPLEMENTER:` staging step.\n1290→- **SKILL.md, Phase 7 closure item 7** carries every `WARNING` line, and adds the FR-7 `--append`\n  step after each leg, for every implementer.\n- **SKILL.md's 5e bullet, and each fix-dispatch step** (v1.3), gain the FR-7 author append at\n  acceptance, ordered before the leg that reviews the code; the 5d bullet gains none.\n- **The SKILL.md teammate-audit bullet** separates audit-leg selection from resolved authorship.\n- **SKILL.md** states the FR-5 re-run trigger: after any agy upgrade, re-run FR-8 step 2 and step\n  2a, and re-take the class-(a) inventory.\n- **`agy-runtime.md` §\"The TDD gate\"** names `h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` and `AGY-GATE:`, and keeps the\n  halt. Its `SessionStart` claim, on two surfaces, is re-checked against the installed agy, which\n  is `1.4.0` at `29ae3e7b`.\n1300→- **The prompt** gets a neutral opening and a `Hook:` line that names each gate by implementer,\n  with no `<`, `>` or `->`.\n- **`state-schema.md` and the schema** get the FR-1 rows, plus the four description rewrites in\n  §\"FR-1\".\n- **`failure-recovery.md`** gets copy 4.\n\n## Components Changed / Added\n\n| Path | Change | FR |\n|---|---|---|\n1310→| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` | five properties; `fallback_agent` and `codex_status` descriptions | FR-1 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_validate.py` | `rfc3339_datetime`, `_semantic_ok` in `classify`, `property_valid` | FR-1, FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` | `Record` fields, `_implementer_tag`, `Implementer`, `resolve_implementer`, author field, `implementer` verb | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` | `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`, author-field parse, FR-3 precedence | FR-3 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_target_identity.py` | receives the 25 moved names | FR-6 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` | guarded import of the 25 names; definitions removed | FR-6 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` (new) | agy write gate | FR-4 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_hook_wiring.py` | `--agy`, `check_agy` | FR-5 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` | `agy` choice, timeout table, check run, docstring, copy 5 | FR-5, FR-8, FR-9 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_write.py` | `--append`; the `APPEND_ONLY` refusal in `merge_fields` | FR-7 |\n1320→| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` | `_review_independence_warnings` | FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` | neutral opening, `Hook:` line, copies 1, 2 and 6 | FR-9 |\n| `h-mad/SKILL.md`, `h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md`, `h-mad/references/state-schema.md`, `h-mad/references/failure-recovery.md` | §\"FR-10\" | FR-9, FR-10 |\n| `.agents/hooks.json` (new, committed by FR-8's stage) | wiring | FR-5, D-2 |\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. FR-1: the schema, the validator predicate and `property_valid`.\n2. FR-2: the resolver and the verb.\n3. FR-3: the line, the hook, the stub re-shape, `ACTIVE_RE`, and the re-anchoring of every row of\n1330→   the two files.\n4. FR-6: the move, the guarded import, the 31 re-pointed rows, and the identity module's anchor\n   recheck.\n5. FR-4, then FR-5.\n6. FR-7: `--append`, then the warnings.\n7. FR-9 and FR-10: the copies, the equivalence test, the corpus, the doc rewrites, then the replay\n   probe.\n8. Merge, then FR-8's stage (OQ-B, spec D-13).\n\nEach Task runs the full h-mad suite, under `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python3`, in the foreground, and\n1340→gates on the summary line.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n| AC | Where |\n|---|---|\n| AC-1.1 | `test_h_mad_state_validate_fallback.py` gains each FR-1 field × value × path (`implementation_authors`'s fixtures are AC-1.3's); `test_h_mad_state_fallback_agent.py` stays green |\n| AC-1.2 | new fixtures beside it: the 5 refused values, the 2 accepted values and the zone-branch fixtures, × 2 paths |\n| AC-1.3 | `test_h_mad_state_validate_fallback.py`, each fixture once per path through `_FORCE_FALLBACK`, as spec v1.9 AC-1.3 lists them: accepted `[]`, one entry per agent (four fixtures), and the three-entry `[m/agy, m/codex, m/agy]` log (duplicates and order kept); refused, each its own fixture, an unknown agent, a missing `agent`, a missing `module`, `\"module\":\"\"`, an extra key, a non-object entry and a non-array value; a record with no `implementation_authors` unchanged; and a refused `--append implementation_authors=…` leaving the store byte-identical (`test_h_mad_state_write.py`) |\n| AC-2.1, AC-2.2 | `test_h_mad_tdd_judge.py`, with `env` and `which` injected; the verb through `_cli` |\n1350→| AC-3.1, AC-3.2 | `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_judge.py` and `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_fallback_agent.py` (re-shaped literals only); new kinds in a new `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_peers.py`; a `bin_dir` with an `agy` stub drives `agy-authorship` |\n| AC-4.1, AC-4.2 | new `test_h_mad_agy_tdd_gate.py`, including the **target differential**: a corpus of target shapes (in-root production `.py`; a test file; `src/test_a.py` hard-linked to `src/z.py`; the allowance file in two case spellings; `docs/x.py`; `/tmp` non-`.py`; `/tmp` `.py`; an outside non-`/tmp` path; an unresolvable path; a production `.py` whose chain holds a `chmod 000` `docs/` that the `rglob` scan cannot see) × `phase5_status` (`active`, `inactive`, `unknown`), each judged by the Codex gate (`Write` with `file_path`, no payload cwd) and by the agy gate (`write_to_file` with `TargetFile`), with the same admit/deny in every cell outside the stated deliberate differences, and the same kind wherever the Codex deny carries one; plus the class-(c) workdir fixtures and the shell differential (§\"FR-4\"); plus, under `inactive`, `run_command` `ls` with `workspacePaths=[]`, `run_command` with no `CommandLine`, and `write_to_file` with `TargetFile: \"\"` each allowed, and the same three under `active` and under `unknown` each denied `kind=judge-error`; plus one fixture per row of §\"FR-4\" \"Every deny\" asserting that row's kind, and a scan of every deny the suite produces asserting exactly one `kind=` token from the closed set |\n| AC-5.1, AC-5.2 | new `test_h_mad_hook_wiring_agy.py` (a `HOME` fixture), plus `test_h_mad_assemble_tdd_agent.py` |\n| AC-6.1 | the existing Codex gate tests unmodified (`test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]` is the import-failure fixture); the new `--self-check` `FAIL policy-import` fixture; the one-`def` test; the `unsafe` tuple parity test; the shell differential |\n| AC-7.1, AC-7.2 | `test_h_mad_state_write.py` (`--append`: the two-entry fixture, the two-appends-in-one-call fixture, the same-key `--set`/`--append` refusal, and the `APPEND_ONLY` refusal once per key with that key alone: `--set review_independence=[]` and `--set implementation_authors=[]`, each exit 2 with the store unchanged) and `test_h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py`; the FR-7 attribution rule is orchestrator prose (SKILL.md, FR-10), pinned by a doc test that the FR-7 step's text states the dispatch as the source; the one code surface that names an author, the `unrecorded` detail text, gets the switch/recovery fixture: `implementer_switch.to == \"agy\"` with a well-formed 5e entry whose `implementer` is `codex`, and the detail must name `codex` and not `agy`; `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)` is `True` and does not raise. AC-7.3's attribution fixtures (spec v1.9: the four of v1.8 plus the pre-field fixture) are each derivable from the record alone, the multi-author recovered one included, since the author set is read from `implementation_authors` (§\"FR-7\", OD-E2 decided); they still have no code surface to drive, since attribution is orchestrator prose, and that surface is owed to the impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\") |\n| AC-8.1, AC-8.2 | probes, §\"FR-8\" |\n| AC-9.1 | `test_h_mad_assemble_tdd_agent.py` `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` is extended: the WIRED fixture (§\"FR-5\") is provisioned in its `tmp_path` root once, before the loop, so all three agents read the same root; the loop becomes `(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\")`; `run_cli` gains an env override so the `agy` run sees the fixture `HOME`; and the assertion becomes `len(hashes) == 3 and len(set(hashes)) == 1`. Today it loops over `(\"codex\", \"grok\")` and asserts `hashes[0] == hashes[1]`, which would leave a third hash unchecked. Plus the union sweep re-run and the three pin files staying green |\n| AC-9.2, AC-9.4 | §\"FR-9\" |\n| AC-9.3 | probe |\n| AC-X | §\"Mutation rows\" |\n1360→\n## Mutation rows (AC-X)\n\nEach new guard below gets one row. The fixture that kills it is named beside it.\n- **FR-1**\n  - `_semantic_ok` call removed from `classify` → `not-a-date` on both paths.\n  - The `datetime` construction removed → `2026-02-30T00:00:00Z`.\n  - `fullmatch` → `match` → `…Zjunk`.\n- **FR-2**\n  - Each `_cause` branch removed → that branch's own fixture, with only that cause present.\n1370→  - The `other` peer step removed → `chosen=codex` out, agy available.\n- **FR-3**\n  - The `implementer-invalid` branch removed → the invalid fixture.\n  - The `INVALID_RECORD` scan stopped at the first record → `[codex-available, invalid]` expects\n    `implementer-invalid`.\n  - The `agy` arm removed → the `agy-authorship` fixture.\n  - The grammar's `peers-out` alternative removed → every stub test.\n- **FR-6**\n  - The import guard removed (a bare top-level import) → `test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]`,\n    whose tree has no identity module: the gate then exits 1 with no JSON.\n1380→  - The self-check's `FAIL policy-import` branch removed → the new self-check fixture, which then\n    sees a `NameError` traceback and exit 1.\n  - Row `G2` itself stays killed through the re-raise (§\"FR-6\", Binding).\n  - No row for removing the `_main_guarded` re-raise, because that mutant is equivalent in\n    decision: without it, every path of `_main_guarded` that can allow first calls a moved name\n    (`_any_phase5_status` runs before any allow), which raises `NameError` into `# M:G2` and\n    denies `judge-error`; the one earlier deny (`M:CX-ROOT-ENTER`) is a deny either way. Only the\n    reason text differs. The re-raise exists so the reason names the import failure.\n- **FR-4**\n  - A class-(a) name moved to (b) or (d) → that class's member fixture.\n1390→  - The class-(d) default replaced by allow → an unknown-name fixture.\n  - The no-path-key deny removed → that fixture.\n  - The `artifactDirectoryPath` `.py` refusal removed → its fixture.\n  - The `finally` deny removed → malformed stdin.\n  - T3 moved after T5 (allowance check before containment) → a `/tmp` non-`.py` write, which then\n    denies `judge-error` instead of allowing.\n  - (v1.4) T2a removed → a `write_to_file` whose `TargetFile` names an existing in-root directory\n    under `active`, which then allows instead of denying `judge-error` (the impl-plan's\n    `od2-directory-target-check-dropped`).\n  - T6 judging `resolved.target` alone instead of every name → the `test_a.py`/`z.py` hard-link\n1400→    fixture.\n  - T6–T7 skipped when `phase5_status == \"inactive\"` → the `chmod 000` `docs/` chain fixture.\n  - T7's `unreadable` branch removed → the same fixture.\n  - T4's `str` check on `artifactDirectoryPath` (`isinstance(adp, str) and adp` → `adp is not\n    None`) → `artifactDirectoryPath: 5` with a non-`.py` target outside both `/tmp` and the root,\n    under `inactive`: the rule allows; the mutant reaches `Path(5)`, raises `TypeError`, and denies\n    `kind=judge-error`. v1.1's fixture (`\"\"`, from a process directory containing the target)\n    could not bite: step 3's `os.chdir(root)` makes `Path(\"\")` the root, and T3 has already sent\n    every in-root target away, so `\"\"` admits nothing either way (design audit cycle 2, codex,\n    run on `_path_within` as a controlled pair). **The empty-string arm is therefore an\n1410→    equivalent mutant at the full gate** and has no row; it stays as defence should step 3's\n    `chdir` move. Residual: that arm is unpinned.\n  - Step 5's `S` condition removed → `run_command` `ls`, `workspacePaths=[]`, `inactive`, which\n    then denies.\n  - Class (c)'s missing-`CommandLine` `S` condition removed → `run_command` with no `CommandLine`,\n    `inactive`, which then denies.\n  - Class (b)'s non-empty-`str` target test weakened to key presence → `TargetFile: \"\"` under\n    `active`, which then allows (no production name) instead of denying `kind=judge-error`.\n  - Each of the three design-owned kinds replaced by `judge-error` at its site\n    (`target-outside-root`, `allowance-file-write`, `shell-not-admitted`) → that row's kind\n1420→    fixture.\n  - Class (c) denying `judge-error` when `cwd` is not an existing directory → `ls` with\n    `Cwd=str(root / \"no-such-dir\")`.\n  - Class (c) joining a relative `Cwd` against the handler's directory → a relative `Cwd` naming\n    a sub-project whose `.venv` interpreter the command uses.\n- **FR-5:** each of the seven reason checks removed → its fixture; `UNWIRED` returning 2 → the\n  AC-5.2 exit fixture.\n- **FR-7**\n  - Each appended value built from `[]` instead of the current value → AC-7.1's two-entry\n    fixture (both earlier entries, compared as `json.dumps` text, must survive).\n1430→  - Accumulation read from `prior` instead of the updated `record` → the two-appends-in-one-call\n    fixture (both earlier entries and both additions, in order).\n  - The same-key `--set`/`--append` refusal removed → its fixture, which expects exit 2 and an\n    unchanged store.\n  - (v1.3) Each `APPEND_ONLY` member removed from the tuple → that key's own `--set …=[]` fixture,\n    run with that key alone, which expects exit 2 and an unchanged store.\n  - v1.0's row \"`--append` mutating the prior list in place\" is dropped: the prior record is\n    discarded after the write, so the persisted bytes are identical in both modes and no\n    observation the suite makes can see it (codex audit cycle 1, run on a controlled pair).\n  - The `independent` consistency check removed → a lying-boolean fixture.\n1440→  - The `unrecorded` trigger restricted to `implementer == \"agy\"` → the `codex` fixture (AC-7.2).\n  - A malformed 6a-prime entry counted as recorded → its fixture.\n  - The `unrecorded` detail text reading `implementer_switch.to` → the switch/recovery fixture.\n  - `property_valid`'s `dict` guard removed (the predicate applied to `value[\"ts\"]` directly) →\n    `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)`, which then raises.\n- **FR-9:** the 8 + 2 rows in §\"FR-9\".\n\n**Existing rows the edits move (E7).** The rule over the class: after each Task, every committed\nmutation row whose `file` the Task edits must still match its `find` exactly once\n(`h_mad_mutation_harness.py --check-anchors`, the harness's own `source.count(find)` test), and a\n1450→row the edit breaks is re-anchored **in that Task**, to the same intent and the same `test`. The\nsweep that found them: every row of `h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/*.json` whose `file` is one this\ndesign edits outside FR-3's and FR-6's files (which §\"FR-3\" and §\"FR-6\" already re-anchor\nwhole), with each `find` located in the file at `cff71b49`:\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `w10a-grok-by-default` (FR-5 Task): its `find` is the `--agent`\n  choices line, which FR-5 rewrites. Re-anchor: `find`\n  `ap.add_argument(\"--agent\", choices=(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\"), default=\"codex\")`, `replace` the\n  same with `default=\"grok\"`, `test` unchanged.\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `t1-timeout-judged-by-value` (FR-5 Task): `find`\n  `args.timeout is not None` sits on the timeout line FR-5 rewrites; the line form in §\"FR-5\"\n1460→  keeps it once, and the `replace` (`args.timeout not in (None, 900)`) still bites\n  `test_agent_grok_explicit_timeout_wins`. No re-anchor if that form is kept.\n- `grok_wire_reverts.json` `wr3-assembler-drops-agent` (FR-5 Task): `find` `        agent=args.agent,`\n  must stay once; the check run FR-5 adds to `main` must not repeat that line.\n- `heartbeat_beat.json` `the-owners-set-no-longer-beats` and `a-bystanders-set-beats-too` (FR-7\n  Task): `find` is `merge_fields`' owner-heartbeat `if` and its assignment; §\"FR-7\" keeps both\n  byte for byte, so no re-anchor. The other two rows of that spec anchor in `beat`, which FR-7\n  does not edit.\n- SKILL.md and `failure-recovery.md` rows: none of their `find` texts lies in a span FR-9/FR-10\n  rewrites (the nearest are `phase7_integrate_blockers_documented.json`'s three rows inside Phase 7\n1470→  item 7 (the closure list, around its 7f integrate step), which the item-7 edit only adds to, and\n  `baseline_sha.json`/`wire_registry_key.json` in §\"Phase 5 (Implementation) sub-steps\" on the 5f\n  bullet, not the 5d bullet FR-9 edits). Every other row on\n  `h_mad_assemble_tdd.py`, `h_mad_state_write.py`, `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` and\n  `h_mad_hook_wiring.py` anchors on code this design does not rewrite. `h_mad_state_validate.py`,\n  `h_mad_state_schema.json` and `codex-implementer-prompt.md` have no rows.\nResidual: the sweep reads the design's edit sites as described here; an implementation that\nrewrites more than it describes moves rows this list does not name, which `--check-anchors` then\ncatches in that Task.\n\n1480→## Residuals\n\nEach is stated where it arises. Collected here:\n- the `which` / `command -v` matrix (FR-2);\n- the verb reads the root only (FR-2);\n- the class-(a) judgement (FR-4);\n- the six-line shell composition in both gates (FR-4);\n- a sibling `overwrite` (FR-4);\n- the review-leg agy is gated too (FR-4);\n- worktree state, not claimed either way (FR-4);\n1490→- an equivalent command spelling (FR-5);\n- a writer that bypasses `_mutate` (FR-7);\n- the deliberate differences from the Codex gate's target sequence, and any rule it gains later\n  (FR-4);\n- relative shell tokens under a `Cwd` that does not exist (FR-4);\n- code a reviewer wrote outside an implementation dispatch (FR-7);\n- prose application (FR-9);\n- a contradicting sentence or a seventh surface (FR-9);\n- (v1.2) a judge kind added to `KINDS` later passes through unlisted (FR-4);\n- (v1.2) T4's empty-string arm is an equivalent mutant, unpinned (Mutation rows);\n1500→- (v1.2) a module missing its 6a-prime entry among recorded ones has no warning of its own (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) no entry is written for a record with no `implementation_authors` field, a module with\n  no well-formed author entry, or a record holding a malformed one (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) the author-before-review ordering is prose, not refused by code (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) a history array added to the schema later and not added to `APPEND_ONLY` (FR-7);\n- (v1.2) rows moved by an edit wider than this design describes (Mutation rows, \"Existing rows\");\n- (v1.4) a class-(b) target ending in `/` that names no existing directory passes T2a and is\n  judged as a file name (FR-4, OD-2);\n- (v1.4) a self-check FAIL added later is classed by the verdict/could-not-run rule, not listed\n  (FR-4 `--self-check`).\n1510→\n## Measurements\n\nTwo behavioural premises carry committed probes under `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`,\neach with its invocation in its docstring and one reading at `200ffd52`:\n- `fr3_state_line_grammar.py` (P-1..P-5, §\"FR-3\"): `PROBE: PASS`;\n- `fr6_import_failure_pair.py` (the hand-built gate trees, §\"FR-6\"): `PROBE: PASS`.\n\nThe census figures below are one reading at `29ae3e7b` each. Their committed probes are owed to\nthe impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\"); the scratch scripts that produced them were deleted,\n1520→and the method is stated beside each figure so a probe can re-derive it.\n\n| Figure | Method | Reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| DO-1a line census | `git ls-files -z h-mad \\| xargs -0 grep -l 'TDD-STATE: active'`, and the plan's four-pattern variant | 6 files; 7 files |\n| M-3, rows over the contract | the plan's pattern over the `find` + `replace` of rows naming the two FR-3 files | 8 rows, 3 specs |\n| rows inside the regions FR-3 rewrites | the `find` offset inside `_read_state`, the authorship block, `_active_records` or `format_state_line` | 13 rows |\n| M-4 over the DO-5 set | the `find` start inside a moved name's `ast` span, for rows naming the Codex gate | 31 of 62 rows, 4 specs |\n| class inventory | the first `init` event's `tools` | 58 names: (a) 11, (b) 5, (c) 1, (d) 41 |\n| live records with FR-1 keys | a key scan over two state files | 0 of 61 records |\n1530→\n## Operator decisions\n\n- **OQ-A — where the shared policy lives (DO-5): decided, spec D-12.** `h_mad_target_identity.py`.\n  A **new** module breaks `test_codex_gate_judge_timeout_reason` unmodified (§\"FR-6\", committed\n  probe). The alternatives v1.0 listed (a new module plus an edited test tree; loading the Codex\n  gate file through `importlib`) are not taken.\n- **OQ-B — FR-8 after the merge (DO-6): decided, spec D-13.** The post-merge stage in §\"FR-8\",\n  with the feature recorded COMPLETE only after it, and this repository's `.agents/hooks.json`\n  committed only on a passed refusal. The override-flag alternative is not taken.\n1540→- **OD-E2 — a durable author record (FR-7): decided 2026-10-16, option (a), spec FR-1 D-15.** The\n  `implementation_authors` field (§\"FR-1\"), appended through `--append` at each accepted\n  implementation dispatch and read as the only source of a module's author set (§\"FR-7\"). Option\n  (b), amending AC-7.3's expected outcome to \"no entry\", is not taken.\n- **OD-2 — a class-(b) directory target: decided 2026-10-16 (operator), impl-plan Task 6.** An\n  existing-directory target is refused `kind=judge-error` under `S` and allowed under `inactive`,\n  as T2a (§\"FR-4\"). Residual: a trailing-`/` path naming no existing directory.\n- **Self-check exits: decided 2026-10-16 (orchestrator, impl-plan cycles 1–2).** A verdict FAIL\n  exits 0 and a could-not-run FAIL exits 2 (§\"FR-4\" `--self-check`); the Codex gate's\n  `FAIL shell-policy` is corrected in impl-plan Task 4.\n1550→\n## Owed by other documents\n\nSpec v1.7 (`c117a695`) settled the v1.0 items it owned: the `codex_status` description pair\n(FR-1), the agy version (FR-8 §\"Version\", `1.4.0` at `200ffd52`), D-12, D-13, D-14 and FR-7\n§\"Attribution\". Still owed:\n- **Plan.** v1.1's plan items (M-4's 31 rows, DO-2's log version, D-12/D-13) are landed in plan\n  v1.6 (`8e242d06`); v1.2 contradicts nothing in it. Plan stage 7's attribution fixture is spec\n  AC-7.3's first; the plan does not yet carry AC-7.3's other three or the E7 re-anchors (§\"Mutation\n  rows\", \"Existing rows the edits move\"), which the impl-plan's FR-5 and FR-7 Tasks must carry.\n1560→- **Spec v1.8 (`bd508fbf`)** adopted the deliberate differences (FR-4), the kind rule, S5 and E4.\n  It names only `judge-error`, `tool-not-admitted` and the judge's kind; the closed set it defers\n  to is §\"FR-4\" \"The deny kinds\" (five gate kinds plus the judge's).\n- **Spec v1.9 (D-15)** carries `implementation_authors`, AC-1.3 and the pre-field fixture, and\n  scopes FR-7's \"no entry\" rule to the three closed cases this design follows. This design adds\n  the `APPEND_ONLY` `--set` refusal over it and over `review_independence` (§\"FR-7\"), which\n  spec v1.9 FR-7 §\"Record\" does not state; the spec owes either that rule or a reason it is out\n  of scope.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.3).** The FR-1 Task carries AC-1.3's `implementation_authors` fixtures; the\n  FR-7 Task carries the two `APPEND_ONLY` fixtures and their mutation row, and AC-7.3's pre-field\n1570→  fixture beside its other four; the FR-10 Task\n  carries the SKILL.md author-append step at 5e GREEN acceptance and at each accepted fix\n  dispatch.\n- **Impl-plan, AC-7.3's surface.** Attribution is orchestrator prose; AC-7.3's five fixtures need\n  a code surface to drive, which spec v1.8 also files as an OPEN-DECISION. OD-E2 leaves this open:\n  it makes the fixtures' inputs durable, not executable.\n- **Spec (v1.4 items).** Lines recording OD-2 (T2a, with its residual); FR-2 naming\n  `step5:implementer_invalid` and `step5:implementer_unresolved`, or adopting them from the\n  impl-plan (§\"FR-2\" \"The caller's halts\"); FR-4/FR-5 self-check: a verdict FAIL exits 0.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.4 item).** The Codex gate's `FAIL parser` is a verdict FAIL that returns 2 like\n1580→  `FAIL shell-policy`; Task 4 corrects only the latter by name. Either Task 4 corrects both, or the\n  impl-plan states why `FAIL parser` stays.\n- **Impl-plan.** These become committed probes: the M-3/M-4 censuses, the class inventory, the FR-9\n  corpus reading and the replay. The FR-3 grammar probe and the FR-6 import-failure probe are\n  committed by this design. Each FR-9/FR-10 Task's RED names the doc-pin census entries it moves.\n\n## Version History\n- v1.0: Initial design (2026-10-16) from spec v1.6 (c853b207) and plan v1.4 (29ae3e7b), tree read at 29ae3e7b. Settles DO-1..DO-7: per-record author field on TDD-STATE (P-1..P-5 probed in Python re and bash 3.2/5.3 ERE); 11-name class-(a) allowlist over the 58-name init.tools inventory; locked --append writer operation; stdlib RFC 3339 predicate in classify on both validator paths, scoped to implementer_switch.ts; 25 moved names into h_mad_target_identity.py with guarded import (M-4 re-derived: 31 rows, 4 specs); HOME-fixture tests and post-merge FR-8 stage; prose-applied carve-out with six per-copy locators and 8 control rows. Two operator questions (OQ-A placement, OQ-B post-merge tracer); codex_status description owed to the spec.\n- v1.1: Design audit cycle 1 (2026-10-16), against spec v1.7 (c117a695), tree at 200ffd52. C1: leap second refused per spec FR-1/D-14, residual framing dropped. C2/C3: FR-4 class (b) is the Codex gate per-target sequence T1-T7 (unresolvable, containment before _is_shell_allowance, every hard-link name for production, read_chain unreadable/inactive branches, no rglob-inactive shortcut per M:G5, non-empty artifactDirectoryPath), deliberate differences listed, target differential test. C4/C11: AC-9.1 WIRED fixture and three-hash assertion. C5: in-place append row dropped as unbitable, replaced by loss and accumulation mutants. C6: FR-7 attribution from accepted implementation dispatches per spec FR-7 Attribution, per-module 6a-prime entries, unrecorded detail text no longer reads implementer_switch. C7: --append accumulates from the updated record; same-key --set/--append refused. C8: import failure re-raised inside _main_guarded so row G2 stays killed; self-check FAIL policy-import. C9: class (c) cwd computed like _command_cwd, chdir only to an existing command directory, no judge-error on a bad Cwd. C10: _semantic_ok never raises; new properties after fallback_agent. M1: committed probes fr3_state_line_grammar.py and fr6_import_failure_pair.py (both PROBE: PASS at 200ffd52). OQ-A/OQ-B recorded as spec D-12/D-13.\n- v1.2: Design audit cycle 2, final corrective revision after the round cap, not re-audited (2026-10-16); spec v1.8 (bd508fbf), plan v1.6 (8e242d06), tree at cff71b49. E1: step-5 workspacePaths cross-check and class (c) missing CommandLine gated on S (active|unknown); every FR-4 deny tabulated with its gating (16 rows). E5: class (b) targets are recognised values that are a non-empty str, '' never canonicalised. E6: closed kind set - judge-error, tool-not-admitted, target-outside-root, allowance-file-write, shell-not-admitted, plus the judge's KINDS passthrough at T7; 'as the Codex gate does' claim corrected (6 of 13 Codex _deny calls kindless). E3: T4 row re-fixtured on a non-str artifactDirectoryPath under inactive; the empty-string arm declared an equivalent mutant (step-3 chdir). E2/E4: authors = accepted 5e GREEN + accepted fix dispatches, never 5d RED; complete set kept in procedure, never rebuilt from entries; lost list -> no entry; OD-E2 (AC-7.3 multi-author recovery needs a durable FR-1 record) to the impl-plan. E7: re-anchor of assemble_tdd_agent w10a-grok-by-default; t1, wr3 and two heartbeat_beat rows kept by stated line forms; --check-anchors rule per Task. E8: property_valid guards dict via _semantic_ok. New rows for the S-gates, the target test, the three design kinds, the dict guard.\n1590→- v1.3: Operator decision OD-E2 option (a) (2026-10-16), aligned to spec v1.9 D-15; tree at 3ad735f7. FR-1: fifth property implementation_authors, array of {module (string, minLength 1), agent (codex|agy|grok|claude)}, both required, no extra keys, placed after review_independence; minLength confirmed in _MiniDraft7's supported set; zero-record reading for the fifth key (54 + 8 records, 0 carrying any of the five keys). FR-7: the author record appended through the existing --append at each accepted 5e GREEN and accepted fix dispatch, never 5d RED, before any review leg of that code runs; the author set and the latest author are read from the field only (v1.2's in-procedure list retired); no entry only for an absent field, a module with no well-formed entry, or a malformed field; the AC-7.3 multi-author recovered and pre-field fixtures derived from durable state. New: APPEND_ONLY --set refusal in merge_fields over review_independence and implementation_authors, with a per-key mutation row (owed to the spec). OD-E2 closed in Operator decisions; Test Plan gains AC-1.3; Residuals, Components, FR-10 and Owed updated. AC-7.3's code surface stays the impl-plan's open decision.\n- v1.4: Owed lines from Phase 5b impl-plan audit cycle 2, final corrective, not re-audited (2026-10-16); impl-plan v1.1 (fc92becf), tree at 84ec2133. Q1: OD-2 recorded as FR-4 T2a (existing-directory target -> judge-error under S, allow under inactive; before T3), deny table 17 rows, deliberate difference, mutation row, residual (trailing '/' naming no directory), Operator decisions. Q2: --self-check rule - a verdict FAIL exits 0, a could-not-run FAIL (policy-import) exits 2; the Codex gate's FAIL shell-policy corrected in impl-plan Task 4, FAIL parser owed. Q3: FR-2 caller halts step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded, step5:implementer_invalid, step5:implementer_unresolved adopted from the impl-plan. Owed: spec lines for all three; impl-plan FAIL parser.\n\nSource spec: # Spec — agy as a peer Phase-5 implementer (`agy-coder-fallback`)\n\n> **Slug note.** The slug predates brainstorm v1.1 and is kept because the state record carries it.\n> agy is a **peer implementer** with Codex's standing, not a fallback.\n\nSource: `docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback-brainstorm.md` v1.1 (operator-approved\n2026-10-16). Every \"currently\" claim below was read from the tree at `a8d9ba99`; the command that\n1600→read it is named beside it.\n\n## Problem\n\nCodex is the only Phase-5 implementer h-mad accepts. The seams that hard-code it are listed here:\n\n- **State.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` declares `codex_status` and `fallback_agent`\n  (`grok|claude|null`) and sets `\"additionalProperties\": false`. Any new key must therefore be\n  declared there, or `h_mad_state_write.py` rejects it. (Read with `cat` on the schema.)\n- **Claude-side authorship gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` refuses Claude's production write\n1610→  as `codex-authorship` when `HMAD_CODEX_UNAVAILABLE` is empty, the state line says\n  `codex-escape=no`, and `command -v codex` succeeds. Otherwise it folds `fallback_agent` into\n  `fallback-grok` / `fallback-invalid`. (`grep -n 'codex-authorship\\|fallback-grok' hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh`.)\n- **Single state source.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` `read_chain` collects every `step5`\n  record on the target's `docs/.bkit-memory.json` chain into `Record(key, codex_status, state_file,\n  fallback)`. `format_state_line` prints `TDD-STATE: active codex-escape=… blocker=… records=…\n  fallback=… record=…`, and the hook parses that line with `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`. The judge's\n  `ESCAPE_STATUSES` is `{\"unavailable\", \"exhausted\"}`.\n- **Staging.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` accepts `--agent` with `choices=(\"codex\",\n  \"grok\")`. The default timeout is 1500 for grok and 900 otherwise. `command_block` derives a\n1620→  non-codex first line from the codex line. The test\n  `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` pins that the prompt bytes do not depend on `--agent`.\n- **Prompt.** `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` opens \"You are Codex implementing…\"\n  and its `Hook:` line names only Codex's and Claude's gates. Because that test pins one prompt\n  for every agent, grok is told it is Codex today.\n- **Write gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` speaks Codex's hook contract. Its\n  `permissionDecision` deny goes out under `hookSpecificOutput`. agy's contract is\n  `{\"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": …}` on stdout (`h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` §\"Hooks\",\n  §\"The TDD gate\"). No agy gate exists, and that section prescribes the halt\n  `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` until one is verified against a real refusal.\n1630→\n## Terms\n\n- **Peer**: `codex` or `agy`. **Fallback**: `fallback_agent`, which is `grok`, `claude`, or\n  absent/`null` (equivalent to `claude`).\n- **Chosen implementer**: the record's `implementer` field. Absent or `null` reads as `codex`.\n- **Resolved implementer**: who actually authors Phase 5 for a record. FR-2 defines it.\n- **Active step5**: at least one record on the governing state chain has `phase == \"step5\"`. This\n  is the same predicate both existing gates use.\n\n1640→## Requirements\n\n### FR-1 — State fields\n\nAdd to `h_mad_state_schema.json`. Every field is OPTIONAL and additive, so `required` does not\nchange and records written before this feature stay valid:\n\n| field | values | absent means |\n|---|---|---|\n| `implementer` | `\"codex\"` \\| `\"agy\"` \\| `null` | `codex` |\n1650→| `agy_status` | `\"available\"` \\| `\"unavailable\"` \\| `\"exhausted\"` \\| `null` | `available` |\n| `implementer_switch` | object `{from, to, reason, ts}` \\| `null` | no switch has happened |\n| `review_independence` | array of objects `{leg, module, reviewer, implementer, independent}` | nothing recorded |\n| `implementation_authors` | array of objects `{module, agent}` (D-15) | no implementation dispatch recorded |\n","absolute_path":"/Users/kimhawk/.grok/sessions/%2FUsers%2Fkimhawk%2F.local%2Fstate%2Fh-mad%2Fgrok-audit-surface%2Frun-ab2c85dc2e25-20261024T132452Z%2Froots%2Fgas-root-d8-s2v1-isogl9ls/01a16e83-9639-7733-9916-502222a5a3fb/prompts/prompt_0.txt","offset":1255,"limit":400,"raw_output":"  `getattr(<mod>, \"<callee>\")` at the RED base.\n- **The missing-symbol role** comes from the fixture's declaration. The test asserts that the\n  exception line names that symbol.\n- **Two classifiers transcribe the two texts.**\n  - `old_rule`: a missing-symbol RED (`ImportError`, `ModuleNotFoundError`, `AttributeError` or\n    `NameError`) is a halt.\n  - `new_rule`: such a RED is valid iff the missing symbol is the caller and the callee resolves.\n  - The test also asserts that `CANONICAL`, imported from the equivalence test, contains\n    `the missing symbol is the caller the task creates` and `the callee resolves at the RED base`.\n    That ties the transcription to the words.\n- **Pass:** the set of cases whose verdict changed equals `{new-caller}`.\n- **Control:** two rows in the same new spec, each run alone. One drops the callee condition, and\n  `both-missing` then changes. The other drops the caller condition, and `other-symbol` and\n  `unrelated-import` then change.\n- The cases' exception lines and verdicts are also written to\n  `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/` as the committed reading.\n\n**The incident replay (AC-9.3).** It is a committed probe under\n`docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`, following FR-9's four steps through `git archive`\nexports, so the live clone is never checked out. The premises were re-checked at `29ae3e7b`:\nHemaSuite `HEAD` is `77fb16f51`, and `531a6296b`, `7aa0d9dec` and `c2d671f6b` are each ancestors\n(`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). Their subjects begin `…Task 4 FR-1 resolver`,\n`…Task 5 FR-5 initiali…` and `…Task 6 CLI surface…`. The probe stamps the HemaSuite sha it reads.\n\n### FR-10 — documentation surfaces\n\nThese follow the spec's FR-10 list and the plan's doc-pin census. Each rewrite keeps every pinned\nliteral the census lists, or changes that test's literal in the same commit.\n- **SKILL.md §\"Codex authors Phase 5 — enforced, not just instructed\"** becomes implementer-neutral.\n  It states FR-2 and FR-3 and names `agy-authorship`, `implementer-invalid` and\n  `h_mad_tdd_judge.py implementer`. The heading and the end anchor\n  `Phase 5 implementation is **Codex's job**` stay, or `_phase_5e_text` and `PHASE5_HEADING` move\n  in the same commit.\n- **SKILL.md §\"Exit-code dispatch for 5d/5e\"** gains a line that holds both `exec agy` and\n  \"implement\", plus the `TDD-IMPLEMENTER:` staging step.\n- **SKILL.md, Phase 7 closure item 7** carries every `WARNING` line, and adds the FR-7 `--append`\n  step after each leg, for every implementer.\n- **SKILL.md's 5e bullet, and each fix-dispatch step** (v1.3), gain the FR-7 author append at\n  acceptance, ordered before the leg that reviews the code; the 5d bullet gains none.\n- **The SKILL.md teammate-audit bullet** separates audit-leg selection from resolved authorship.\n- **SKILL.md** states the FR-5 re-run trigger: after any agy upgrade, re-run FR-8 step 2 and step\n  2a, and re-take the class-(a) inventory.\n- **`agy-runtime.md` §\"The TDD gate\"** names `h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` and `AGY-GATE:`, and keeps the\n  halt. Its `SessionStart` claim, on two surfaces, is re-checked against the installed agy, which\n  is `1.4.0` at `29ae3e7b`.\n- **The prompt** gets a neutral opening and a `Hook:` line that names each gate by implementer,\n  with no `<`, `>` or `->`.\n- **`state-schema.md` and the schema** get the FR-1 rows, plus the four description rewrites in\n  §\"FR-1\".\n- **`failure-recovery.md`** gets copy 4.\n\n## Components Changed / Added\n\n| Path | Change | FR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` | five properties; `fallback_agent` and `codex_status` descriptions | FR-1 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_validate.py` | `rfc3339_datetime`, `_semantic_ok` in `classify`, `property_valid` | FR-1, FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` | `Record` fields, `_implementer_tag`, `Implementer`, `resolve_implementer`, author field, `implementer` verb | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` | `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`, author-field parse, FR-3 precedence | FR-3 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_target_identity.py` | receives the 25 moved names | FR-6 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` | guarded import of the 25 names; definitions removed | FR-6 |\n| `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` (new) | agy write gate | FR-4 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_hook_wiring.py` | `--agy`, `check_agy` | FR-5 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` | `agy` choice, timeout table, check run, docstring, copy 5 | FR-5, FR-8, FR-9 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_write.py` | `--append`; the `APPEND_ONLY` refusal in `merge_fields` | FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` | `_review_independence_warnings` | FR-7 |\n| `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` | neutral opening, `Hook:` line, copies 1, 2 and 6 | FR-9 |\n| `h-mad/SKILL.md`, `h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md`, `h-mad/references/state-schema.md`, `h-mad/references/failure-recovery.md` | §\"FR-10\" | FR-9, FR-10 |\n| `.agents/hooks.json` (new, committed by FR-8's stage) | wiring | FR-5, D-2 |\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. FR-1: the schema, the validator predicate and `property_valid`.\n2. FR-2: the resolver and the verb.\n3. FR-3: the line, the hook, the stub re-shape, `ACTIVE_RE`, and the re-anchoring of every row of\n   the two files.\n4. FR-6: the move, the guarded import, the 31 re-pointed rows, and the identity module's anchor\n   recheck.\n5. FR-4, then FR-5.\n6. FR-7: `--append`, then the warnings.\n7. FR-9 and FR-10: the copies, the equivalence test, the corpus, the doc rewrites, then the replay\n   probe.\n8. Merge, then FR-8's stage (OQ-B, spec D-13).\n\nEach Task runs the full h-mad suite, under `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python3`, in the foreground, and\ngates on the summary line.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n| AC | Where |\n|---|---|\n| AC-1.1 | `test_h_mad_state_validate_fallback.py` gains each FR-1 field × value × path (`implementation_authors`'s fixtures are AC-1.3's); `test_h_mad_state_fallback_agent.py` stays green |\n| AC-1.2 | new fixtures beside it: the 5 refused values, the 2 accepted values and the zone-branch fixtures, × 2 paths |\n| AC-1.3 | `test_h_mad_state_validate_fallback.py`, each fixture once per path through `_FORCE_FALLBACK`, as spec v1.9 AC-1.3 lists them: accepted `[]`, one entry per agent (four fixtures), and the three-entry `[m/agy, m/codex, m/agy]` log (duplicates and order kept); refused, each its own fixture, an unknown agent, a missing `agent`, a missing `module`, `\"module\":\"\"`, an extra key, a non-object entry and a non-array value; a record with no `implementation_authors` unchanged; and a refused `--append implementation_authors=…` leaving the store byte-identical (`test_h_mad_state_write.py`) |\n| AC-2.1, AC-2.2 | `test_h_mad_tdd_judge.py`, with `env` and `which` injected; the verb through `_cli` |\n| AC-3.1, AC-3.2 | `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_judge.py` and `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_fallback_agent.py` (re-shaped literals only); new kinds in a new `test_h_mad_tdd_gate_peers.py`; a `bin_dir` with an `agy` stub drives `agy-authorship` |\n| AC-4.1, AC-4.2 | new `test_h_mad_agy_tdd_gate.py`, including the **target differential**: a corpus of target shapes (in-root production `.py`; a test file; `src/test_a.py` hard-linked to `src/z.py`; the allowance file in two case spellings; `docs/x.py`; `/tmp` non-`.py`; `/tmp` `.py`; an outside non-`/tmp` path; an unresolvable path; a production `.py` whose chain holds a `chmod 000` `docs/` that the `rglob` scan cannot see) × `phase5_status` (`active`, `inactive`, `unknown`), each judged by the Codex gate (`Write` with `file_path`, no payload cwd) and by the agy gate (`write_to_file` with `TargetFile`), with the same admit/deny in every cell outside the stated deliberate differences, and the same kind wherever the Codex deny carries one; plus the class-(c) workdir fixtures and the shell differential (§\"FR-4\"); plus, under `inactive`, `run_command` `ls` with `workspacePaths=[]`, `run_command` with no `CommandLine`, and `write_to_file` with `TargetFile: \"\"` each allowed, and the same three under `active` and under `unknown` each denied `kind=judge-error`; plus one fixture per row of §\"FR-4\" \"Every deny\" asserting that row's kind, and a scan of every deny the suite produces asserting exactly one `kind=` token from the closed set |\n| AC-5.1, AC-5.2 | new `test_h_mad_hook_wiring_agy.py` (a `HOME` fixture), plus `test_h_mad_assemble_tdd_agent.py` |\n| AC-6.1 | the existing Codex gate tests unmodified (`test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]` is the import-failure fixture); the new `--self-check` `FAIL policy-import` fixture; the one-`def` test; the `unsafe` tuple parity test; the shell differential |\n| AC-7.1, AC-7.2 | `test_h_mad_state_write.py` (`--append`: the two-entry fixture, the two-appends-in-one-call fixture, the same-key `--set`/`--append` refusal, and the `APPEND_ONLY` refusal once per key with that key alone: `--set review_independence=[]` and `--set implementation_authors=[]`, each exit 2 with the store unchanged) and `test_h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py`; the FR-7 attribution rule is orchestrator prose (SKILL.md, FR-10), pinned by a doc test that the FR-7 step's text states the dispatch as the source; the one code surface that names an author, the `unrecorded` detail text, gets the switch/recovery fixture: `implementer_switch.to == \"agy\"` with a well-formed 5e entry whose `implementer` is `codex`, and the detail must name `codex` and not `agy`; `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)` is `True` and does not raise. AC-7.3's attribution fixtures (spec v1.9: the four of v1.8 plus the pre-field fixture) are each derivable from the record alone, the multi-author recovered one included, since the author set is read from `implementation_authors` (§\"FR-7\", OD-E2 decided); they still have no code surface to drive, since attribution is orchestrator prose, and that surface is owed to the impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\") |\n| AC-8.1, AC-8.2 | probes, §\"FR-8\" |\n| AC-9.1 | `test_h_mad_assemble_tdd_agent.py` `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` is extended: the WIRED fixture (§\"FR-5\") is provisioned in its `tmp_path` root once, before the loop, so all three agents read the same root; the loop becomes `(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\")`; `run_cli` gains an env override so the `agy` run sees the fixture `HOME`; and the assertion becomes `len(hashes) == 3 and len(set(hashes)) == 1`. Today it loops over `(\"codex\", \"grok\")` and asserts `hashes[0] == hashes[1]`, which would leave a third hash unchecked. Plus the union sweep re-run and the three pin files staying green |\n| AC-9.2, AC-9.4 | §\"FR-9\" |\n| AC-9.3 | probe |\n| AC-X | §\"Mutation rows\" |\n\n## Mutation rows (AC-X)\n\nEach new guard below gets one row. The fixture that kills it is named beside it.\n- **FR-1**\n  - `_semantic_ok` call removed from `classify` → `not-a-date` on both paths.\n  - The `datetime` construction removed → `2026-02-30T00:00:00Z`.\n  - `fullmatch` → `match` → `…Zjunk`.\n- **FR-2**\n  - Each `_cause` branch removed → that branch's own fixture, with only that cause present.\n  - The `other` peer step removed → `chosen=codex` out, agy available.\n- **FR-3**\n  - The `implementer-invalid` branch removed → the invalid fixture.\n  - The `INVALID_RECORD` scan stopped at the first record → `[codex-available, invalid]` expects\n    `implementer-invalid`.\n  - The `agy` arm removed → the `agy-authorship` fixture.\n  - The grammar's `peers-out` alternative removed → every stub test.\n- **FR-6**\n  - The import guard removed (a bare top-level import) → `test_codex_gate_kind[judge-error]`,\n    whose tree has no identity module: the gate then exits 1 with no JSON.\n  - The self-check's `FAIL policy-import` branch removed → the new self-check fixture, which then\n    sees a `NameError` traceback and exit 1.\n  - Row `G2` itself stays killed through the re-raise (§\"FR-6\", Binding).\n  - No row for removing the `_main_guarded` re-raise, because that mutant is equivalent in\n    decision: without it, every path of `_main_guarded` that can allow first calls a moved name\n    (`_any_phase5_status` runs before any allow), which raises `NameError` into `# M:G2` and\n    denies `judge-error`; the one earlier deny (`M:CX-ROOT-ENTER`) is a deny either way. Only the\n    reason text differs. The re-raise exists so the reason names the import failure.\n- **FR-4**\n  - A class-(a) name moved to (b) or (d) → that class's member fixture.\n  - The class-(d) default replaced by allow → an unknown-name fixture.\n  - The no-path-key deny removed → that fixture.\n  - The `artifactDirectoryPath` `.py` refusal removed → its fixture.\n  - The `finally` deny removed → malformed stdin.\n  - T3 moved after T5 (allowance check before containment) → a `/tmp` non-`.py` write, which then\n    denies `judge-error` instead of allowing.\n  - (v1.4) T2a removed → a `write_to_file` whose `TargetFile` names an existing in-root directory\n    under `active`, which then allows instead of denying `judge-error` (the impl-plan's\n    `od2-directory-target-check-dropped`).\n  - T6 judging `resolved.target` alone instead of every name → the `test_a.py`/`z.py` hard-link\n    fixture.\n  - T6–T7 skipped when `phase5_status == \"inactive\"` → the `chmod 000` `docs/` chain fixture.\n  - T7's `unreadable` branch removed → the same fixture.\n  - T4's `str` check on `artifactDirectoryPath` (`isinstance(adp, str) and adp` → `adp is not\n    None`) → `artifactDirectoryPath: 5` with a non-`.py` target outside both `/tmp` and the root,\n    under `inactive`: the rule allows; the mutant reaches `Path(5)`, raises `TypeError`, and denies\n    `kind=judge-error`. v1.1's fixture (`\"\"`, from a process directory containing the target)\n    could not bite: step 3's `os.chdir(root)` makes `Path(\"\")` the root, and T3 has already sent\n    every in-root target away, so `\"\"` admits nothing either way (design audit cycle 2, codex,\n    run on `_path_within` as a controlled pair). **The empty-string arm is therefore an\n    equivalent mutant at the full gate** and has no row; it stays as defence should step 3's\n    `chdir` move. Residual: that arm is unpinned.\n  - Step 5's `S` condition removed → `run_command` `ls`, `workspacePaths=[]`, `inactive`, which\n    then denies.\n  - Class (c)'s missing-`CommandLine` `S` condition removed → `run_command` with no `CommandLine`,\n    `inactive`, which then denies.\n  - Class (b)'s non-empty-`str` target test weakened to key presence → `TargetFile: \"\"` under\n    `active`, which then allows (no production name) instead of denying `kind=judge-error`.\n  - Each of the three design-owned kinds replaced by `judge-error` at its site\n    (`target-outside-root`, `allowance-file-write`, `shell-not-admitted`) → that row's kind\n    fixture.\n  - Class (c) denying `judge-error` when `cwd` is not an existing directory → `ls` with\n    `Cwd=str(root / \"no-such-dir\")`.\n  - Class (c) joining a relative `Cwd` against the handler's directory → a relative `Cwd` naming\n    a sub-project whose `.venv` interpreter the command uses.\n- **FR-5:** each of the seven reason checks removed → its fixture; `UNWIRED` returning 2 → the\n  AC-5.2 exit fixture.\n- **FR-7**\n  - Each appended value built from `[]` instead of the current value → AC-7.1's two-entry\n    fixture (both earlier entries, compared as `json.dumps` text, must survive).\n  - Accumulation read from `prior` instead of the updated `record` → the two-appends-in-one-call\n    fixture (both earlier entries and both additions, in order).\n  - The same-key `--set`/`--append` refusal removed → its fixture, which expects exit 2 and an\n    unchanged store.\n  - (v1.3) Each `APPEND_ONLY` member removed from the tuple → that key's own `--set …=[]` fixture,\n    run with that key alone, which expects exit 2 and an unchanged store.\n  - v1.0's row \"`--append` mutating the prior list in place\" is dropped: the prior record is\n    discarded after the write, so the persisted bytes are identical in both modes and no\n    observation the suite makes can see it (codex audit cycle 1, run on a controlled pair).\n  - The `independent` consistency check removed → a lying-boolean fixture.\n  - The `unrecorded` trigger restricted to `implementer == \"agy\"` → the `codex` fixture (AC-7.2).\n  - A malformed 6a-prime entry counted as recorded → its fixture.\n  - The `unrecorded` detail text reading `implementer_switch.to` → the switch/recovery fixture.\n  - `property_valid`'s `dict` guard removed (the predicate applied to `value[\"ts\"]` directly) →\n    `property_valid(\"implementer_switch\", None)`, which then raises.\n- **FR-9:** the 8 + 2 rows in §\"FR-9\".\n\n**Existing rows the edits move (E7).** The rule over the class: after each Task, every committed\nmutation row whose `file` the Task edits must still match its `find` exactly once\n(`h_mad_mutation_harness.py --check-anchors`, the harness's own `source.count(find)` test), and a\nrow the edit breaks is re-anchored **in that Task**, to the same intent and the same `test`. The\nsweep that found them: every row of `h-mad/tests/mutation-specs/*.json` whose `file` is one this\ndesign edits outside FR-3's and FR-6's files (which §\"FR-3\" and §\"FR-6\" already re-anchor\nwhole), with each `find` located in the file at `cff71b49`:\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `w10a-grok-by-default` (FR-5 Task): its `find` is the `--agent`\n  choices line, which FR-5 rewrites. Re-anchor: `find`\n  `ap.add_argument(\"--agent\", choices=(\"codex\", \"grok\", \"agy\"), default=\"codex\")`, `replace` the\n  same with `default=\"grok\"`, `test` unchanged.\n- `assemble_tdd_agent.json` `t1-timeout-judged-by-value` (FR-5 Task): `find`\n  `args.timeout is not None` sits on the timeout line FR-5 rewrites; the line form in §\"FR-5\"\n  keeps it once, and the `replace` (`args.timeout not in (None, 900)`) still bites\n  `test_agent_grok_explicit_timeout_wins`. No re-anchor if that form is kept.\n- `grok_wire_reverts.json` `wr3-assembler-drops-agent` (FR-5 Task): `find` `        agent=args.agent,`\n  must stay once; the check run FR-5 adds to `main` must not repeat that line.\n- `heartbeat_beat.json` `the-owners-set-no-longer-beats` and `a-bystanders-set-beats-too` (FR-7\n  Task): `find` is `merge_fields`' owner-heartbeat `if` and its assignment; §\"FR-7\" keeps both\n  byte for byte, so no re-anchor. The other two rows of that spec anchor in `beat`, which FR-7\n  does not edit.\n- SKILL.md and `failure-recovery.md` rows: none of their `find` texts lies in a span FR-9/FR-10\n  rewrites (the nearest are `phase7_integrate_blockers_documented.json`'s three rows inside Phase 7\n  item 7 (the closure list, around its 7f integrate step), which the item-7 edit only adds to, and\n  `baseline_sha.json`/`wire_registry_key.json` in §\"Phase 5 (Implementation) sub-steps\" on the 5f\n  bullet, not the 5d bullet FR-9 edits). Every other row on\n  `h_mad_assemble_tdd.py`, `h_mad_state_write.py`, `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` and\n  `h_mad_hook_wiring.py` anchors on code this design does not rewrite. `h_mad_state_validate.py`,\n  `h_mad_state_schema.json` and `codex-implementer-prompt.md` have no rows.\nResidual: the sweep reads the design's edit sites as described here; an implementation that\nrewrites more than it describes moves rows this list does not name, which `--check-anchors` then\ncatches in that Task.\n\n## Residuals\n\nEach is stated where it arises. Collected here:\n- the `which` / `command -v` matrix (FR-2);\n- the verb reads the root only (FR-2);\n- the class-(a) judgement (FR-4);\n- the six-line shell composition in both gates (FR-4);\n- a sibling `overwrite` (FR-4);\n- the review-leg agy is gated too (FR-4);\n- worktree state, not claimed either way (FR-4);\n- an equivalent command spelling (FR-5);\n- a writer that bypasses `_mutate` (FR-7);\n- the deliberate differences from the Codex gate's target sequence, and any rule it gains later\n  (FR-4);\n- relative shell tokens under a `Cwd` that does not exist (FR-4);\n- code a reviewer wrote outside an implementation dispatch (FR-7);\n- prose application (FR-9);\n- a contradicting sentence or a seventh surface (FR-9);\n- (v1.2) a judge kind added to `KINDS` later passes through unlisted (FR-4);\n- (v1.2) T4's empty-string arm is an equivalent mutant, unpinned (Mutation rows);\n- (v1.2) a module missing its 6a-prime entry among recorded ones has no warning of its own (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) no entry is written for a record with no `implementation_authors` field, a module with\n  no well-formed author entry, or a record holding a malformed one (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) the author-before-review ordering is prose, not refused by code (FR-7);\n- (v1.3) a history array added to the schema later and not added to `APPEND_ONLY` (FR-7);\n- (v1.2) rows moved by an edit wider than this design describes (Mutation rows, \"Existing rows\");\n- (v1.4) a class-(b) target ending in `/` that names no existing directory passes T2a and is\n  judged as a file name (FR-4, OD-2);\n- (v1.4) a self-check FAIL added later is classed by the verdict/could-not-run rule, not listed\n  (FR-4 `--self-check`).\n\n## Measurements\n\nTwo behavioural premises carry committed probes under `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`,\neach with its invocation in its docstring and one reading at `200ffd52`:\n- `fr3_state_line_grammar.py` (P-1..P-5, §\"FR-3\"): `PROBE: PASS`;\n- `fr6_import_failure_pair.py` (the hand-built gate trees, §\"FR-6\"): `PROBE: PASS`.\n\nThe census figures below are one reading at `29ae3e7b` each. Their committed probes are owed to\nthe impl-plan (§\"Owed by other documents\"); the scratch scripts that produced them were deleted,\nand the method is stated beside each figure so a probe can re-derive it.\n\n| Figure | Method | Reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| DO-1a line census | `git ls-files -z h-mad \\| xargs -0 grep -l 'TDD-STATE: active'`, and the plan's four-pattern variant | 6 files; 7 files |\n| M-3, rows over the contract | the plan's pattern over the `find` + `replace` of rows naming the two FR-3 files | 8 rows, 3 specs |\n| rows inside the regions FR-3 rewrites | the `find` offset inside `_read_state`, the authorship block, `_active_records` or `format_state_line` | 13 rows |\n| M-4 over the DO-5 set | the `find` start inside a moved name's `ast` span, for rows naming the Codex gate | 31 of 62 rows, 4 specs |\n| class inventory | the first `init` event's `tools` | 58 names: (a) 11, (b) 5, (c) 1, (d) 41 |\n| live records with FR-1 keys | a key scan over two state files | 0 of 61 records |\n\n## Operator decisions\n\n- **OQ-A — where the shared policy lives (DO-5): decided, spec D-12.** `h_mad_target_identity.py`.\n  A **new** module breaks `test_codex_gate_judge_timeout_reason` unmodified (§\"FR-6\", committed\n  probe). The alternatives v1.0 listed (a new module plus an edited test tree; loading the Codex\n  gate file through `importlib`) are not taken.\n- **OQ-B — FR-8 after the merge (DO-6): decided, spec D-13.** The post-merge stage in §\"FR-8\",\n  with the feature recorded COMPLETE only after it, and this repository's `.agents/hooks.json`\n  committed only on a passed refusal. The override-flag alternative is not taken.\n- **OD-E2 — a durable author record (FR-7): decided 2026-10-16, option (a), spec FR-1 D-15.** The\n  `implementation_authors` field (§\"FR-1\"), appended through `--append` at each accepted\n  implementation dispatch and read as the only source of a module's author set (§\"FR-7\"). Option\n  (b), amending AC-7.3's expected outcome to \"no entry\", is not taken.\n- **OD-2 — a class-(b) directory target: decided 2026-10-16 (operator), impl-plan Task 6.** An\n  existing-directory target is refused `kind=judge-error` under `S` and allowed under `inactive`,\n  as T2a (§\"FR-4\"). Residual: a trailing-`/` path naming no existing directory.\n- **Self-check exits: decided 2026-10-16 (orchestrator, impl-plan cycles 1–2).** A verdict FAIL\n  exits 0 and a could-not-run FAIL exits 2 (§\"FR-4\" `--self-check`); the Codex gate's\n  `FAIL shell-policy` is corrected in impl-plan Task 4.\n\n## Owed by other documents\n\nSpec v1.7 (`c117a695`) settled the v1.0 items it owned: the `codex_status` description pair\n(FR-1), the agy version (FR-8 §\"Version\", `1.4.0` at `200ffd52`), D-12, D-13, D-14 and FR-7\n§\"Attribution\". Still owed:\n- **Plan.** v1.1's plan items (M-4's 31 rows, DO-2's log version, D-12/D-13) are landed in plan\n  v1.6 (`8e242d06`); v1.2 contradicts nothing in it. Plan stage 7's attribution fixture is spec\n  AC-7.3's first; the plan does not yet carry AC-7.3's other three or the E7 re-anchors (§\"Mutation\n  rows\", \"Existing rows the edits move\"), which the impl-plan's FR-5 and FR-7 Tasks must carry.\n- **Spec v1.8 (`bd508fbf`)** adopted the deliberate differences (FR-4), the kind rule, S5 and E4.\n  It names only `judge-error`, `tool-not-admitted` and the judge's kind; the closed set it defers\n  to is §\"FR-4\" \"The deny kinds\" (five gate kinds plus the judge's).\n- **Spec v1.9 (D-15)** carries `implementation_authors`, AC-1.3 and the pre-field fixture, and\n  scopes FR-7's \"no entry\" rule to the three closed cases this design follows. This design adds\n  the `APPEND_ONLY` `--set` refusal over it and over `review_independence` (§\"FR-7\"), which\n  spec v1.9 FR-7 §\"Record\" does not state; the spec owes either that rule or a reason it is out\n  of scope.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.3).** The FR-1 Task carries AC-1.3's `implementation_authors` fixtures; the\n  FR-7 Task carries the two `APPEND_ONLY` fixtures and their mutation row, and AC-7.3's pre-field\n  fixture beside its other four; the FR-10 Task\n  carries the SKILL.md author-append step at 5e GREEN acceptance and at each accepted fix\n  dispatch.\n- **Impl-plan, AC-7.3's surface.** Attribution is orchestrator prose; AC-7.3's five fixtures need\n  a code surface to drive, which spec v1.8 also files as an OPEN-DECISION. OD-E2 leaves this open:\n  it makes the fixtures' inputs durable, not executable.\n- **Spec (v1.4 items).** Lines recording OD-2 (T2a, with its residual); FR-2 naming\n  `step5:implementer_invalid` and `step5:implementer_unresolved`, or adopting them from the\n  impl-plan (§\"FR-2\" \"The caller's halts\"); FR-4/FR-5 self-check: a verdict FAIL exits 0.\n- **Impl-plan (v1.4 item).** The Codex gate's `FAIL parser` is a verdict FAIL that returns 2 like\n  `FAIL shell-policy`; Task 4 corrects only the latter by name. Either Task 4 corrects both, or the\n  impl-plan states why `FAIL parser` stays.\n- **Impl-plan.** These become committed probes: the M-3/M-4 censuses, the class inventory, the FR-9\n  corpus reading and the replay. The FR-3 grammar probe and the FR-6 import-failure probe are\n  committed by this design. Each FR-9/FR-10 Task's RED names the doc-pin census entries it moves.\n\n## Version History\n- v1.0: Initial design (2026-10-16) from spec v1.6 (c853b207) and plan v1.4 (29ae3e7b), tree read at 29ae3e7b. Settles DO-1..DO-7: per-record author field on TDD-STATE (P-1..P-5 probed in Python re and bash 3.2/5.3 ERE); 11-name class-(a) allowlist over the 58-name init.tools inventory; locked --append writer operation; stdlib RFC 3339 predicate in classify on both validator paths, scoped to implementer_switch.ts; 25 moved names into h_mad_target_identity.py with guarded import (M-4 re-derived: 31 rows, 4 specs); HOME-fixture tests and post-merge FR-8 stage; prose-applied carve-out with six per-copy locators and 8 control rows. Two operator questions (OQ-A placement, OQ-B post-merge tracer); codex_status description owed to the spec.\n- v1.1: Design audit cycle 1 (2026-10-16), against spec v1.7 (c117a695), tree at 200ffd52. C1: leap second refused per spec FR-1/D-14, residual framing dropped. C2/C3: FR-4 class (b) is the Codex gate per-target sequence T1-T7 (unresolvable, containment before _is_shell_allowance, every hard-link name for production, read_chain unreadable/inactive branches, no rglob-inactive shortcut per M:G5, non-empty artifactDirectoryPath), deliberate differences listed, target differential test. C4/C11: AC-9.1 WIRED fixture and three-hash assertion. C5: in-place append row dropped as unbitable, replaced by loss and accumulation mutants. C6: FR-7 attribution from accepted implementation dispatches per spec FR-7 Attribution, per-module 6a-prime entries, unrecorded detail text no longer reads implementer_switch. C7: --append accumulates from the updated record; same-key --set/--append refused. C8: import failure re-raised inside _main_guarded so row G2 stays killed; self-check FAIL policy-import. C9: class (c) cwd computed like _command_cwd, chdir only to an existing command directory, no judge-error on a bad Cwd. C10: _semantic_ok never raises; new properties after fallback_agent. M1: committed probes fr3_state_line_grammar.py and fr6_import_failure_pair.py (both PROBE: PASS at 200ffd52). OQ-A/OQ-B recorded as spec D-12/D-13.\n- v1.2: Design audit cycle 2, final corrective revision after the round cap, not re-audited (2026-10-16); spec v1.8 (bd508fbf), plan v1.6 (8e242d06), tree at cff71b49. E1: step-5 workspacePaths cross-check and class (c) missing CommandLine gated on S (active|unknown); every FR-4 deny tabulated with its gating (16 rows). E5: class (b) targets are recognised values that are a non-empty str, '' never canonicalised. E6: closed kind set - judge-error, tool-not-admitted, target-outside-root, allowance-file-write, shell-not-admitted, plus the judge's KINDS passthrough at T7; 'as the Codex gate does' claim corrected (6 of 13 Codex _deny calls kindless). E3: T4 row re-fixtured on a non-str artifactDirectoryPath under inactive; the empty-string arm declared an equivalent mutant (step-3 chdir). E2/E4: authors = accepted 5e GREEN + accepted fix dispatches, never 5d RED; complete set kept in procedure, never rebuilt from entries; lost list -> no entry; OD-E2 (AC-7.3 multi-author recovery needs a durable FR-1 record) to the impl-plan. E7: re-anchor of assemble_tdd_agent w10a-grok-by-default; t1, wr3 and two heartbeat_beat rows kept by stated line forms; --check-anchors rule per Task. E8: property_valid guards dict via _semantic_ok. New rows for the S-gates, the target test, the three design kinds, the dict guard.\n- v1.3: Operator decision OD-E2 option (a) (2026-10-16), aligned to spec v1.9 D-15; tree at 3ad735f7. FR-1: fifth property implementation_authors, array of {module (string, minLength 1), agent (codex|agy|grok|claude)}, both required, no extra keys, placed after review_independence; minLength confirmed in _MiniDraft7's supported set; zero-record reading for the fifth key (54 + 8 records, 0 carrying any of the five keys). FR-7: the author record appended through the existing --append at each accepted 5e GREEN and accepted fix dispatch, never 5d RED, before any review leg of that code runs; the author set and the latest author are read from the field only (v1.2's in-procedure list retired); no entry only for an absent field, a module with no well-formed entry, or a malformed field; the AC-7.3 multi-author recovered and pre-field fixtures derived from durable state. New: APPEND_ONLY --set refusal in merge_fields over review_independence and implementation_authors, with a per-key mutation row (owed to the spec). OD-E2 closed in Operator decisions; Test Plan gains AC-1.3; Residuals, Components, FR-10 and Owed updated. AC-7.3's code surface stays the impl-plan's open decision.\n- v1.4: Owed lines from Phase 5b impl-plan audit cycle 2, final corrective, not re-audited (2026-10-16); impl-plan v1.1 (fc92becf), tree at 84ec2133. Q1: OD-2 recorded as FR-4 T2a (existing-directory target -> judge-error under S, allow under inactive; before T3), deny table 17 rows, deliberate difference, mutation row, residual (trailing '/' naming no directory), Operator decisions. Q2: --self-check rule - a verdict FAIL exits 0, a could-not-run FAIL (policy-import) exits 2; the Codex gate's FAIL shell-policy corrected in impl-plan Task 4, FAIL parser owed. Q3: FR-2 caller halts step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded, step5:implementer_invalid, step5:implementer_unresolved adopted from the impl-plan. Owed: spec lines for all three; impl-plan FAIL parser.\n\nSource spec: # Spec — agy as a peer Phase-5 implementer (`agy-coder-fallback`)\n\n> **Slug note.** The slug predates brainstorm v1.1 and is kept because the state record carries it.\n> agy is a **peer implementer** with Codex's standing, not a fallback.\n\nSource: `docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback-brainstorm.md` v1.1 (operator-approved\n2026-10-16). Every \"currently\" claim below was read from the tree at `a8d9ba99`; the command that\nread it is named beside it.\n\n## Problem\n\nCodex is the only Phase-5 implementer h-mad accepts. The seams that hard-code it are listed here:\n\n- **State.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_state_schema.json` declares `codex_status` and `fallback_agent`\n  (`grok|claude|null`) and sets `\"additionalProperties\": false`. Any new key must therefore be\n  declared there, or `h_mad_state_write.py` rejects it. (Read with `cat` on the schema.)\n- **Claude-side authorship gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh` refuses Claude's production write\n  as `codex-authorship` when `HMAD_CODEX_UNAVAILABLE` is empty, the state line says\n  `codex-escape=no`, and `command -v codex` succeeds. Otherwise it folds `fallback_agent` into\n  `fallback-grok` / `fallback-invalid`. (`grep -n 'codex-authorship\\|fallback-grok' hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh`.)\n- **Single state source.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_tdd_judge.py` `read_chain` collects every `step5`\n  record on the target's `docs/.bkit-memory.json` chain into `Record(key, codex_status, state_file,\n  fallback)`. `format_state_line` prints `TDD-STATE: active codex-escape=… blocker=… records=…\n  fallback=… record=…`, and the hook parses that line with `STATE_ACTIVE_RE`. The judge's\n  `ESCAPE_STATUSES` is `{\"unavailable\", \"exhausted\"}`.\n- **Staging.** `h-mad/scripts/h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` accepts `--agent` with `choices=(\"codex\",\n  \"grok\")`. The default timeout is 1500 for grok and 900 otherwise. `command_block` derives a\n  non-codex first line from the codex line. The test\n  `test_prompt_file_is_agent_independent` pins that the prompt bytes do not depend on `--agent`.\n- **Prompt.** `h-mad/references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` opens \"You are Codex implementing…\"\n  and its `Hook:` line names only Codex's and Claude's gates. Because that test pins one prompt\n  for every agent, grok is told it is Codex today.\n- **Write gate.** `h-mad/hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py` speaks Codex's hook contract. Its\n  `permissionDecision` deny goes out under `hookSpecificOutput`. agy's contract is\n  `{\"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": …}` on stdout (`h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` §\"Hooks\",\n  §\"The TDD gate\"). No agy gate exists, and that section prescribes the halt\n  `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` until one is verified against a real refusal.\n\n## Terms\n\n- **Peer**: `codex` or `agy`. **Fallback**: `fallback_agent`, which is `grok`, `claude`, or\n  absent/`null` (equivalent to `claude`).\n- **Chosen implementer**: the record's `implementer` field. Absent or `null` reads as `codex`.\n- **Resolved implementer**: who actually authors Phase 5 for a record. FR-2 defines it.\n- **Active step5**: at least one record on the governing state chain has `phase == \"step5\"`. This\n  is the same predicate both existing gates use.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### FR-1 — State fields\n\nAdd to `h_mad_state_schema.json`. Every field is OPTIONAL and additive, so `required` does not\nchange and records written before this feature stay valid:\n\n| field | values | absent means |\n|---|---|---|\n| `implementer` | `\"codex\"` \\| `\"agy\"` \\| `null` | `codex` |\n| `agy_status` | `\"available\"` \\| `\"unavailable\"` \\| `\"exhausted\"` \\| `null` | `available` |\n| `implementer_switch` | object `{from, to, reason, ts}` \\| `null` | no switch has happened |\n| `review_independence` | array of objects `{leg, module, reviewer, implementer, independent}` | nothing recorded |\n| `implementation_authors` | array of objects `{module, agent}` (D-15) | no implementation dispatch recorded |\n\n","total_lines":4391}},"locations":[]}
