nvariants.base.md` §\"Guard"},{"line_number":2433,"content":"  so `h-mad/invariants.base.md` §\"Incident replay\" applies, and the synthetic corpus above does not"},{"line_number":3004,"content":"   invariants P-1..P-5 in DO-1a. Those are assertions on the judge's **real** output, not on stubs,"},{"line_number":3017,"content":"   discipline** (`h-mad/invariants.base.md` §\"Audit-gate signal discipline\": a normal verdict,"},{"line_number":3119,"content":"   case (`h-mad/invariants.base.md` §\"Guard narrowing\", §\"Incident replay\")."},{"line_number":3241,"content":"  and its shape must satisfy the placement invariants P-1..P-5 (see DO-1a)."},{"line_number":3255,"content":"  **Placement invariants — design constraints on the new line.** Each is an assertion on"},{"line_number":3283,"content":"  **What the invariants leave open.** This was probed at `d90decc6` with a scratch script, since"},{"line_number":3295,"content":"  five invariants are binding, and the design chooses a shape that keeps all five. The free slot is"},{"line_number":3810,"content":"  - choose the `TDD-STATE:` shape: no optional peer fields, the five placement invariants"},{"line_number":3837,"content":"- v1.2: Plan audit cycle 1 and spec v1.4 at e6610381 (2026-10-16). F1: stage 5 mirrors the FR-5 exit table and AC-5.2 (verdicts exit 0, UNREADABLE and no-token exit 2; token and exit code pinned separately; assembler docstring rewritten). F2: DO-4 premise corrected (format is enforced on neither path, probed at d90decc6); the mechanism is a design obligation, with the rfc3339-validator hazard, the AC-1.2 fixtures and classify_store for a schema-wide mechanism. F3/F4: stage 6 adds the old/new differential corpus (AC-9.2, changed set = {new-caller}) and the HemaSuite T4/T5/T6 incident replay (AC-9.3); new DO-7 says where the rule is applied. F5: stage 8 adds step 2a, the forced handler timeout (AC-8.2), and R-13. F6: DO-1a corrected; placement invariants P-1..P-5 over 6 tests, probed; the per-record slot is free and no header field may follow fallback=. F7: the Phase-7 locator is a str.index slice, not titled_section; the doc-pin census covers every rewritten section, including the _phas [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":3858,"content":"### Base invariants (workflow-universal; non-overridable by any project file — but the operator `## Acknowledged-not-fixed` sidecar still applies to base findings):"},{"line_number":3863,"content":"> `INLINE_BASE_INVARIANTS` slot (name written bare — a bracketed mention inside an inlined"},{"line_number":3866,"content":"> per-project `<PROJECT_ROOT>/.h-mad/invariants.md` domain layer. These rules apply to every"},{"line_number":3868,"content":"> invariants file may add domain rules but may not downgrade or delete a base rule. The"},{"line_number":4025,"content":"## Guard narrowing"},{"line_number":4193,"content":"### Project invariants (domain rules for this repository):"},{"line_number":4198,"content":"> workflow-universal `invariants.base.md`. The base layer already enforces the"}]}]},"locations":[]}
