nder active/unknown, allowed under inactive; FR-4 deliberate difference 6, AC-4.1 fixture; residual: trailing-/ path naming no existing directory. P2 -> FR-2 halts named: step5:implementer_invalid (invalid), step5:implementer_unresolved (no-record, unreadable), step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded (record=failed); adopted from impl-plan Task 16; failure-recovery.md rows not added (residual). P3 -> FR-5: the gate's --self-check verdict FAIL prints its token on stdout and exits 0, operational error nonzero; Codex gate FAIL shell-policy corrected in impl-plan Task 4; Codex FAIL parser residual; AC-5.2 gains the self-check fixture and mutant. P4 -> FR-9 Hook line keeps Claude's h-mad-tdd-gate.sh (test_hook_line_names_both_gates). Owed: design FR-4/FR-2 lines.\n","content_concise":"1180→  Reason: design v1.2 (OD-E2) showed AC-7.3's \"multi-author, recovered\" fixture could not pass\n  without a durable author record, because the assembler's prompt, out and log files are under\n  `/tmp` and its slug names no agent. The fixture stays as written and now has its source. The\n  rejected option (b) was to amend the fixture to \"no entry\".\n- **D-16 Directory target refused under active step5 (OD-2, operator decision, 2026-10-16):** a\n  class-(b) target that names an existing directory is refused with `kind=judge-error` when the\n  scan reads `active` or `unknown`, and allowed when it reads `inactive` (FR-4 deliberate\n  difference 6). Reason: impl-plan v1.1 Task 6 showed that `canonicalise` returns no name and\n  no `unresolvable` flag for `.`, `src/`, `src` and the root, so the class-(b) sequence would\n  otherwise allow a directory target under `active`. Residual: a trailing-`/` path that names no\n1190→  existing directory is not covered and is judged as a file name.\n\n## Open questions for the operator\n\nNone — OQ-1/OQ-2 settled 2026-10-16; the design's OQ-A/OQ-B settled 2026-10-16 (D-12, D-13);\nthe design's OD-E2 settled 2026-10-16 (D-15); the impl-plan's OD-2 settled 2026-10-16 (D-16).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Per-task implementer selection. It can come later on the same field.\n1200→- Refusing a peer's production write in that peer's own gate when the other peer is the resolved\n  implementer, for example a Codex verifier dispatch writing production code under\n  `implementer=agy`. Residual: the test-first judge still applies, and the per-dispatch\n  `git status --short` diff (agy-runtime.md §\"Author and reviewer roles\") is what shows it.\n- A write-time gate for grok, and authorship rules for agy as the orchestrating host.\n- Routing audit legs by `agy_status`.\n\n## Owed by other documents\n\nNone of these are edited by this spec.\n1210→- `h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` says there is no `SessionStart` on two surfaces:\n  - §\"Hooks\" (\"There is **no `SessionStart`**\");\n  - the §\"Construct mapping\" table's `hook-event` row (\"there is no `SessionStart`\").\n\n  agy's current hooks.md lists `SessionStart` as a supported event. Both surfaces need a re-check\n  against the installed agy (`agy --version` prints 1.4.0 at `200ffd52`), they are corrected\n  together, and the correction stamps the version it was checked against.\n  (`grep -n 'SessionStart' h-mad/references/agy-runtime.md` at `200ffd52`: 2 matching lines, one\n  under each heading.) Residual: this is a content predicate, so a third restatement added later\n  is found only by re-running the grep.\n1220→- **Design (v1.8 items).** FR-4: enumerate the closed kind list and give every deny path a member\n  (E6); its claim that `unknown` \"denies `kind=judge-error`, as the Codex gate does for a shell\n  command\" is false at `cff71b49` — the Codex gate's `unknown` shell deny carries no `kind=`\n  token. FR-7: name where the complete author set is kept (E2) and correct \"the GREEN dispatch the\n  orchestrator accepted at 5d\" to 5e (E4).\n- **Design (v1.9, D-15).** FR-1: add `implementation_authors` with FR-1's entry schema to the\n  schema JSON and a `state-schema.md` row. FR-7: retire \"the complete set is kept in the\n  procedure\" and OD-E2 in favour of reading the set from `implementation_authors`; the\n  `--append` mechanism (DO-3) must accept this key with the same guarantees, and the \"When the\n  dispatch list is lost\" rule becomes FR-7's three closed unrecoverable cases.\n1230→- **Design (spec v1.10).** FR-4: record D-16 as a directory check before the target is judged,\n  and add it to §\"Deliberate differences\" as item 6; FR-4 `--self-check`: a verdict `FAIL` exits\n  0 (replacing \"a nonzero exit\"), and the Codex gate's `FAIL shell-policy` is corrected in impl-plan\n  Task 4; FR-2: adopt the halts `step5:implementer_invalid` and `step5:implementer_unresolved`.\n- **Impl-plan.** AC-7.3's surface (FR-7 §\"Attribution\" must have code to drive, or the AC is an\n  OPEN-DECISION), now including the pre-field fixture; AC-1.3's fixtures; AC-4.1's `unknown`\n  fixtures and AC-4.2's per-deny-path kind fixtures.\n- **Plan.** If the plan carries FR-1's field list or AC-7.3's fixtures, it gains\n  `implementation_authors`, AC-1.3 and the pre-field fixture.\n\n1240→## Version History\n- v1.0: Initial spec (2026-10-16) from brainstorm v1.1. Settles 8 open questions (D-1..D-8): run_command takes the Codex command-shape rule, not a stated residual; per-project .agents/hooks.json; root from handler cwd; provisional 1500 s timeout then tracer formula; PATH+status+env availability; feature-only implementer; flag in state; audit legs unchanged. Folds brief fix 3 (#8) WIRE-PIN new-caller RED case as FR-9. OQ-1 (Codex-reviews-Codex flag), OQ-2 (.agents exclude) for the operator.\n- v1.1: Operator decisions 2026-10-16 (2026-10-16). OQ-1 -> D-9: FR-7 flag fires for any reviewer == implementer, Codex reviewing Codex included; warning only. OQ-2 -> D-10: operator narrowed .git/info/exclude /.agents/ to /.agents/skills/ (check-ignore evidence at d65374e9), no git add -f; per-clone residual stated. Open questions section now empty.\n- v1.2: Operator decision 2026-10-16 -> D-11: FR-7 review_independence_unrecorded widened from agy-only to every implementer (codex|agy|grok|claude), matching D-9; warning only. Trigger pinned to a 6a-prime leg that ran (archreview READY_TO_MERGE|WITH_FIXES|NO) with no leg=6a-prime entry; other archreview values already surface. Pre-existing features settled: no grandfather rule, archived features untouched (no batch caller). AC-7.2 added.\n- v1.3: Plan-author findings against v1.2 (2026-10-16). FR-3: a missing state-line field refuses judge-error (tree precedent: missing-field fixture), so the two gate stub-line fixtures are re-shaped with assertions byte-identical — the AC-3.2 exception; test_h_mad_tdd_judge.py ACTIVE_RE and line-quoting mutation rows follow the line. FR-7: writer has no append (--set replaces); add-without-loss is a requirement, mechanism a design obligation; AC-7.1 gains the two-entry fixture. FR-6: rows re-pointed to the shared module, then ALL_CAUGHT; moved names stay bound on the Codex gate module. FR-9/AC-9.1/FR-10: failure-recovery.md red_wrong_reason row; rule surfaces closed with sweep. FR-1/FR-10/AC-1.1: fallback_agent description on schema JSON and state-schema.md, pinned literals named. Owed: second SessionStart surface (Construct-mapping hook-event row). All ACs reformatted to the h_mad_ac_census.py grammar (- **AC-n.m:**).\n- v1.4: Plan audit cycle 1 findings owned by the spec (2026-10-16). F1 -> FR-5 exit-code table: AGY-GATE WIRED/UNWIRED (all seven reasons, no-hooks-file included) exit 0 and the assembler's agy_tdd_hook_unverified verdict HALT exits 0; UNREADABLE and a no-token check exit 2; existing assembler HALTs keep exit 2 (residual); AC-5.2. F2 -> FR-1: .ts is RFC 3339 date-time; neither validator path enforces format today (probed), so refusal on both paths is the requirement and the mechanism a design obligation; rfc3339-validator hazard; residual for started_ts/owner_heartbeat_ts/halt_ts; AC-1.2. F3 -> FR-9 differential corpus over