d the assembler's agy_tdd_hook_unverified verdict HALT exits 0; UNREADABLE and a no-token check exit 2; existing assembler HALTs keep exit 2 (residual); AC-5.2. F2 -> FR-1: .ts is RFC 3339 date-time; neither validator path enforces format today (probed), so refusal on both paths is the requirement and the mechanism a design obligation; rfc3339-validator hazard; residual for started_ts/owner_heartbeat_ts/halt_ts; AC-1.2. F3 -> FR-9 differential corpus over four missing-symbol cases, changed set == {new-caller}; AC-9.2. F4 -> FR-9 incident replay of HemaSuite notebooklm F-3 (T4/T5 WIRE-PIN 1, T6 WIRE-PIN 2) with wire-cut re-run; AC-9.3. F5 -> FR-8 step 2a forced handler timeout with four classified outcomes; step 2 now settles two unknowns; FR-5 re-run trigger includes it; AC-8.2. F6 -> no contradiction; FR-3 now lists the real-line assertions (two in test_h_mad_tdd_gate_fallback_agent.py, four tests in test_h_mad_tdd_judge.py) as placement constraints; AC-3.2 extended.\n- v1.5: Plan audit cycle 2 findings owned by the spec, final corrective revision after the round cap (2026-10-16). B -> FR-10 adds the SKILL.md teammate-audit bullet: audit-leg selection vs resolved authorship (Claude only when resolved=claude), anchor prefix and the four pinned tokens kept. C -> FR-9 surface census gains surface 5, the h_mad_assemble_tdd.py assemble() wiring header (split string literals), and its pin test_h_mad_assemble_tdd.py TestWiringShape.test_the_pin_is_told_what_its_red_must_be; the census method now joins Python adjacent literals via ast and collapses markdown whitespace, measured at 9c3b799d; residual: run-time-built strings. AC-9.1 lists the header. D -> FR-9 replay and AC-9.3 name all three pins with files and commits (531a6296b, 7aa0d9dec, c2d671f6b); T5/T6 replay evaluates the direct-call / two-argument getattr form; the committed scaffolded RED (AssertionError) is recorded as old-verdict valid, correcting the false old-verdict=halt claim. A -> new AC-9.4: the six rule copies bound to one authority, with a per-copy control.\n- v1.6: Advisory delta review of plan v1.3 (608e430), spec-owned parts (2026-10-16). Should-fix 3 -> FR-9: the joined reading (ast str constants) is blind to non-str text in a .py file; axis named with three members (comments, files ast.parse rejects, bytes literals). The sweep is now the union of the line grep and the joined reading, which adds joined .py comment tokens; parse failures are reported as unparsed=N and read by hand; residual: run-time-built strings and a bytes literal split across lines. Measured at 5f72c2f3: union 7 files, line-grep-minus-joined 0, comment hits 0 (incidental), unparsed=0. AC-9.1 re-run is the union and reports unparsed=N. Must-fix 1 (spec side) and Should-fix 4 -> AC-9.4: the carve-out text is the whole three-sentence FR-9 block; each copy is read from its own source location, never from the assembled prompt or a file-level contains-check over a file holding more than one copy; a locator matching zero or several spans fails the test; the control mutates exactly one copy, runs once per copy and once per sentence in at least one copy, with a find unique in its file (mutation harness anchor_status), the .py find written against source bytes including the literal split.\n- v1.7: Design audit cycle 1, spec-owned items (2026-10-16). S1 (codex C1) -> FR-1/AC-1.1/AC-1.2 + D-14: .ts narrowed to seconds 00-59, a leap second (2016-12-31T23:59:60Z) refused on both paths; reason: every .ts comes from Python datetime via the writer, which cannot hold second 60 (orchestrator decision). S2 (codex C6) -> FR-7 Attribution: an entry's implementer is the author of the reviewed code, from its successful implementation dispatch, never implementer_switch.to (historical) or the implementer field; multi-author code is non-independent if the reviewer is any author. S3 -> FR-1/FR-10/AC-1.1: codex_status schema description and state-schema.md row rewritten to FR-2 authorship (no test pins the text; the fallback_agent-after-codex_status order pin stated); FR-8 Version: 1.4.0 at 200ffd52, each reading stamps its version; Owed SessionStart re-check re-stamped 1.4.0 at 200ffd52; FR-6/AC-6.1 shared module = h_mad_target_identity.py (D-12, OQ-A); FR-8/AC-8.1 post-merge stage, COMPLETE only after it (D-13, OQ-B). Open questions: OQ-A/OQ-B settled.\n- v1.8: Design audit cycle 2, final corrective revision after the round cap, not re-audited (2026-10-16). S1/E6 -> FR-4 'Every deny carries a kind': rule over every deny path, closed list owned by the design, spec names only judge-error, tool-not-admitted and the judge's Verdict kind; Codex gate has 6 of 13 kindless _deny call sites at cff71b49. E1 -> FR-4 'The activity reading': three-valued scan (active/unknown/inactive), every step5-gated deny also fires on unknown, class-(b) production .py still read through read_chain under inactive; workspacePaths and Tool classes sentences re-worded. E5 -> FR-4 Target keys: a non-empty-string value counts as no path key. S4 -> FR-4 'Deliberate differences from the Codex gate': design's four adopted plus the kind rule as a fifth. S2/E2/E4 -> FR-7 Attribution sub-bullets (5e GREEN + accepted fixes, never 5d RED; complete author set, never a projection) and new AC-7.3. S5 -> adopted: reviewer none of the authors names the latest accepted dispatch's author. S3 -> leap-second ValueError quote drops the version-dependent tail. AC-4.1/AC-4.2 extended; FR-6 states the unknown-scan shell deny; Owed gains design and impl-plan items.\n- v1.9: Operator decision OD-E2 (a) (2026-10-16) -> D-15: FR-1 gains implementation_authors, an optional array of {module, agent} (agent codex|agy|grok|claude; module non-empty string; no extra keys), appended never altered through FR-7's Record mechanism on accepting a 5e GREEN or fix dispatch, never 5d RED or a halted/timed-out/rejected dispatch; duplicates kept, array order = acceptance order. New AC-1.3 (valid entries accepted, unknown agent and other malformed shapes refused, both validator paths). FR-7 Attribution reads the author set from the field on every leg; unrecoverable cases closed to three (field absent: pre-field features; no entry for the module: a record-step defect; malformed) -> no entry. AC-7.3 multi-author fixture unchanged with its source named; pre-field fixture added. AC-7.2 'only FR-1 field' narrowed to routing field. FR-10 SKILL.md Phase-5 step bullet. Owed: design FR-1/FR-7 (retire procedure-kept set and OD-E2), impl-plan AC-1.3 + pre-field fixture, plan mirror.\n- v1.10: Owed lines from impl-plan v1.1 (Phase 5b), final corrective revision, not re-audited (2026-10-16). P1 -> D-16 (OD-2, operator): a class-(b) target naming an existing directory denies kind=judge-error under active/unknown, allowed under inactive; FR-4 deliberate difference 6, AC-4.1 fixture; residual: trailing-/ path naming no existing directory. P2 -> FR-2 halts named: step5:implementer_invalid (invalid), step5:implementer_unresolved (no-record, unreadable), step5:implementer_switch_unrecorded (record=failed); adopted from impl-plan Task 16; failure-recovery.md rows not added (residual). P3 -> FR-5: the gate's --self-check verdict FAIL prints its token on stdout and exits 0, operational error nonzero; Codex gate FAIL shell-policy corrected in impl-plan Task 4; Codex FAIL parser residual; AC-5.2 gains the self-check fixture and mutant. P4 -> FR-9 Hook line keeps Claude's h-mad-tdd-gate.sh (test_hook_line_names_both_gates). Owed: design FR-4/FR-2 lines.\n","total_lines":1251}},"locations":[]}
{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-07b964bb-3010-413c-99c8-05ac9938675c-14","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"960→  second), the `codex_status` surfaces in FR-1, and FR-7's Attribution rule. Open for the spec:\n  AC-7.1 and AC-7.2 do not name the Attribution fixture (stored `implementer_switch.to=agy`,\n  Codex-authored code, Codex reviewer → `independent=false`). The plan carries it in stage 7. If\n  it should be an acceptance criterion, the spec owes it.\n- **Design.** DO-1 through DO-7. Design v1.0 (`df46f72a`) addresses all seven; its audit cycle 1\n  findings are the design's own revision and are not restated here:\n  - choose the `TDD-STATE:` shape: no optional peer fields, the five placement invariants\n    P-1..P-5 held, and any gate test whose asserted outcome no new-shape stub can reach reported\n    (DO-1, DO-1a);\n  - name the `review_independence` add mechanism and, for a read-modify-write, its lost-entry\n970→    detection (DO-3);\n  - pick the `.ts` refusal mechanism, cite the probe, carry the `rfc3339-validator` hazard, and\n    if the mechanism is schema-wide, run `classify_store` over the live state files (DO-4);\n  - fix the moved-name set and keep the names an existing test reaches bound on the Codex gate\n    module (DO-5);\n  - say whether the FR-9 carve-out stays prose-applied or gains a check, and state the corpus\n    residual that follows. Place the AC-9.4 equivalence test, which the plan has named, give each\n    of the six copies its own locator so that a single-copy mutation fails the test, and fix its\n    canonical carve-out block (all three sentences) to spec FR-9's text (DO-7).\n- **Impl-plan.** Each FR-9/FR-10 Task's RED names the doc-pin census entries it moves (R-8). The\n980→  doc-pin census, the DO-1a line census and the M-4 row census become committed probes under\n  `docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`.\n- **A later feature.** Classify the assembler's existing `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT` reasons as verdict\n  or operational error (spec v1.4 FR-5 residual).\n\n## Next Steps\n\nThe Phase-3 audit cycle runs on two surfaces, and revisions go back to `plan-author`. The\noperator then reviews and approves. The design obligations DO-1..DO-7 are inputs to Phase 4.\n\n990→## Version History\n- v1.0: Initial plan (2026-10-16) from spec v1.2 at 17d73037. Carries D-9/D-11 for every implementer, D-10 per-clone prerequisite, design obligations DO-1..DO-6 (state-line shape and its literals, read-only allowlist, review_independence append, schema constructs on both validator paths, shell-policy module boundary, installed-path vs worktree), mutation re-anchoring risks R-1/R-3, and six items owed by the spec.\n- v1.1: Re-synced to spec v1.3 at e7730f78 (2026-10-16). DO-1a/R-4 closed to the AC-3.2 stub-line exception (missing field = judge-error; the keep-old-stubs branch is removed). DO-3, stage 7 and R-5 now carry FR-7's add requirement. DO-5, stage 4 and R-3 keep the moved names bound on the Codex gate module, with rows re-pointed then ALL_CAUGHT. Stage 6 adds the failure-recovery.md 5d row and the test_h_mad_agent_definitions.py pin. Stage 1 adds the four pinned fallback_agent substrings. R-8 adds the two SKILL.md heading pins. Success Criteria now gate FR-10. The halt-token census is re-scoped to h-mad/ (3 files). All spec items under Owed are marked answered.\n- v1.2: Plan audit cycle 1 and spec v1.4 at e6610381 (2026-10-16). F1: stage 5 mirrors the FR-5 exit table and AC-5.2 (verdicts exit 0, UNREADABLE and no-token exit 2; token and exit code pinned separately; assembler docstring rewritten). F2: DO-4 premise corrected (format is enforced on neither path, probed at d90decc6); the mechanism is a design obligation, with the rfc3339-validator hazard, the AC-1.2 fixtures and classify_store for a schema-wide mechanism. F3/F4: stage 6 adds the old/new differential corpus (AC-9.2, changed set = {new-caller}) and the HemaSuite T4/T5/T6 incident replay (AC-9.3); new DO-7 says where the rule is applied. F5: stage 8 adds step 2a, the forced handler timeout (AC-8.2), and R-13. F6: DO-1a corrected; placement invariants P-1..P-5 over 6 tests, probed; the per-record slot is free and no header field may follow fallback=. F7: the Phase-7 locator is a str.index slice, not titled_section; the doc-pin census covers every rewritten section, including the _phase_5e_text end anchor; R-8 is rewritten. S1: each FR-10 baseline carries its command, re-run at d90decc6. ACs are now 18.\n- v1.3: Final corrective revision after the plan audit round cap: cycle-2 build findings only, and spec v1.5 at e8def13f (2026-10-16). A: stage 6 and DO-7 bind the six copies of the FR-9 carve-out to one authority (AC-9.4). The plan names the equivalence test and carries a one-copy-per-row mutation control. B: stage 6 rewrites the SKILL.md teammate-audit bullet to separate audit-leg selection from resolved authorship (resolved = claude), and pins the replacement condition (baseline 0/0 at 9c3b799d); Success Criteria lists it. C: the FR-9 census adds surface 5, the h_mad_assemble_tdd.py assemble() wiring header, and its pin in test_h_mad_assemble_tdd.py. The census states the split-across-a-line-break class and its joined-literal sweep (7 files at 9c3b799d). D: the incident replay names the three pin files and commits, and replays T5/T6 in direct-call form, recording the scaffolded RED. E: the doc-pin census adds the missed pins from test_h_mad_tdd_gate_docs.py and test_grok_fallback_docs.py, files the _skill_gate_bullet pin under the teammate section, and becomes a candidate list with stated residuals; the R-8 over-claim is removed. ACs are now 19.\n- v1.4: Answers the advisory delta review of v1.3 (2026-10-16), no new scope. Must-fix 1 and Should-fix 1: stage 6 and DO-7 no longer read the assembler copy from the assembled wiring prompt; each of the six copies is read from its own source location (each template copy located individually, the .py copy from its joined str constant), the locators are a DO-7 obligation that must make a single-copy mutation fail the test, and each mutation row's find carries context unique in its file because the harness refuses a non-unique anchor. Should-fix 2: canonical carve-out sentence becomes the canonical carve-out block (all three sentences of spec FR-9's block) at stage 6, DO-7 and the Design owed line. Should-fix 3: the FR-9 census states that the joined-literal reading cannot see .py comments or parse failures, the AC-9.1 re-run takes the union with the line grep, re-measured at 5f72c2f3 (union 7 files, comment hits 0, parse failures 0), and the spec item is listed as owed. Should-fix 4: DO-7's residual now matches the census (a run-time-built surface is found only by reading the dispatch-building code). Should-fix 5: the doc-pin census files test_h_mad_extract_verdict.py and test_h_mad_portable_timeout.py under the prompt (eleven of 14 carry a pin; three stay unclassified). Nit: the copies' formats are restated (four markdown shapes and one Python form).\n- v1.5: Answers the plan items of the design audit cycle 1 decision sheet (design v1.0 at df46f72a), no new scope (2026-10-16). P1: M-4 re-derived at 200ffd52 over the DO-5 set design v1.0 fixes (25 names): 31 of 62 Codex-gate rows in 4 specs; the 10-function closure alone reproduces the retired 19; R-3 restated, its row file corrected to hooks/h-mad-codex-tdd-gate.py. P2: DO-2 no longer asks for the inventory log agy version, which the log does not record; the class-(a) list is re-checked against an init.tools inventory re-captured with agy --version (design: FR-8 step 1). P3: OQ-A (policy in h_mad_target_identity.py) mirrored in stage 4 and DO-5; OQ-B (post-merge FR-8 stage, COMPLETE only after it) mirrored in DO-6 and R-2. P4: agy 1.4.0 at 200ffd52 in the Overview and R-9. The stale spec FR-9 residual owed item is dropped (spec v1.6 states it) and the FR-9 census paragraph cites it; the spec owed list now carr