d the tests' seam. Then FR-5's table applies:\n- `WIRED` → continue to PASS;\n- `UNWIRED` → print `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified`, then the check line indented by\n  two spaces, as existing HALT details are. Write no prompt, exit 2;\n- `UNREADABLE` → the same two lines, exit 2;\n- no `AGY-GATE:` line, or a timeout → `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified check=no-token`,\n  exit 2.\n\nThe verdict branch does not raise `Halt`, because every `Halt` exits 2. The module docstring's\n`exit 0 on PASS, 2 on any HALT` becomes: `exit 0 on PASS and on HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified after\nAGY-GATE: UNWIRED; 2 on every other HALT`. A test pins that sentence, and a test pins that the old\none is absent. `command_block`'s existing prefix rewrite already emits `hmad-dispatch exec agy`, and\n`exec agy` accepts `--model`, `--effort` and `--timeout` (`hmad-dispatch.sh` `_cmd_exec`).\n\n**DO-6: no override path in code.**\n- **Tests.** Tests of `check_agy` set `HOME` to a fixture directory holding\n  `.gemini/config/skills/h-mad/hooks/h-mad-agy-tdd-gate.py` as a symlink to the gate under test.\n  `os.path.expanduser` honours `HOME`, so the shipped code has no worktree switch.\n- **Any test that runs the assembler with `--agent agy` and expects a prompt** needs that `HOME`\n  fixture **and** a `<root>/.agents/hooks.json` holding FR-5's exact entry in its project root.\n","total_lines":1489}},"locations":[]}
{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-d287e7f5-4491-40ab-954e-4bb8d8347961-25","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"990→  enumerates is driven by its own fixture, and each fixture asserts that `reason` ends with\n  exactly one `kind=<kind>` whose value is in the design's closed list (FR-4 §\"Every deny carries\n  a kind\"); a deny path with no fixture, or a kind outside the list, fails the AC.\n- **AC-5.1:** The wiring check emits each `UNWIRED` reason from its own fixture. `--agent agy`\n  writes no prompt and halts on each of them.\n- **AC-5.2:** Each row of FR-5's exit-code table is pinned by its own fixture, and each fixture\n  asserts the stdout token and the exit code separately:\n  - an `UNWIRED` fixture (one per reason, reusing AC-5.1's) shows check exit 0, and assembler\n    `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified` with exit 0;\n  - a `hooks.json` holding invalid JSON shows check `UNREADABLE` with exit 2, and the assembler\n1000→    HALT with exit 2;\n  - a check stubbed to print no token shows the assembler `HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified check=no-token`\n    with exit 2;\n  - `WIRED` shows exit 0 on both;\n  - the agy gate's `--self-check` with a verdict `FAIL` forced prints that `FAIL` token on stdout\n    with exit 0, and the wiring check reads it as `UNWIRED reason=self-check-failed`.\n\n  A mutation that returns 2 on `UNWIRED` is killed, and so is one that returns 2 on a self-check\n  verdict `FAIL`.\n- **AC-6.1:** The shell policy is imported, not copied: one definition in the tree. The Codex gate's\n1010→  existing shell tests pass unmodified. Every mutation row re-pointed under FR-6 runs\n  `MUTATION: ALL_CAUGHT` against the shared module, `h_mad_target_identity.py` (D-12). The agy gate refuses each `unsafe` command in the Codex\n  gate's `--self-check` list.\n- **AC-7.1:** `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` emits each of the three FR-7 warnings from its own\n  fixture, and none of them moves `ready`. Adding a `review_independence` entry to a record that\n  already holds two leaves both earlier entries byte-identical. An entry that fails FR-1 is\n  refused, and the store is unchanged.\n- **AC-7.2:** `review_independence_unrecorded` fires, with no `leg=6a-prime` entry, for each\n  implementer `codex` (field absent included), `agy`, `grok` and `claude`, each from its own\n  fixture (`grok` and `claude` through `implementer_switch.to`, the only FR-1 routing field that takes them; `implementation_authors` is an authorship record and does not trigger the warning), and for each `archreview` value `READY_TO_MERGE`, `WITH_FIXES` and `NO`. It does not fire"}}],"rawOutput":{"type":"ReadFile","FileContent":{"content":"990→  enumerates is driven by its own fixture, and each fixture asserts that `reason` ends with\n  exactly one `kind=<kind>` whose value is in the design's closed list (FR-4 §\"Every deny carries\n  a kind\"); a deny path with no fixture, or a kind outside the list, fails the AC.\n- **AC-5.1:** The wiring check emits each `UNWIRED` reason from its own fixture. `--agent agy`\n  writes no prompt and halts on each of them.\n- **AC-5.2:** Each row of FR-5's exit-code table is pinned by its own fixture, and each fixture\n  asserts the stdout token and the exit code separately:\n  - an `UNWIRED` fixture (one per reason, reusing AC-5.1's) shows check exit 0, and assembler\n    `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified` with exit 0;\n  - a `hooks.json` holding invalid JSON shows check `UNREADABLE` with exit 2, and the assembler\n1000→    HALT with exit 2;\n  - a check stubbed to print no token shows the assembler `HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified check=no-token`\n    with exit 2;\n  - `WIRED` shows exit 0 on both;\n  - the agy gate's `--self-check` with a verdict `FAIL` forced prints that `FAIL` token on stdout\n    with exit 0, and the wiring check reads it as `UNWIRED reason=self-check-failed`.\n\n  A mutation that returns 2 on `UNWIRED` is killed, and so is one that returns 2 on a self-check\n  verdict `FAIL`.\n- **AC-6.1:** The shell policy is imported, not copied: one definition in the tree. The Codex gate's\n1010→  existing shell tests pass unmodified. Every mutation row re-pointed under FR-6 runs\n  `MUTATION: ALL_CAUGHT` against the shared module, `h_mad_target_identity.py` (D-12). The agy gate refuses each `unsafe` command in the Codex\n  gate's `--self-check` list.\n- **AC-7.1:** `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` emits each of the three FR-7 warnings from its own\n  fixture, and none of them moves `ready`. Adding a `review_independence` entry to a record that\n  already holds two leaves both earlier entries byte-identical. An entry that fails FR-1 is\n  refused, and the store is unchanged.\n- **AC-7.2:** `review_independence_unrecorded` fires, with no `leg=6a-prime` entry, for each\n  implementer `codex` (field absent included), `agy`, `grok` and `claude`, each from its own\n  fixture (`grok` and `claude` through `implementer_switch.to`, the only FR-1 routing field that takes them; `implementation_authors` is an authorship record and does not trigger the warning), and for each `archreview` value `READY_TO_MERGE`, `WITH_FIXES` and `NO`. It does not fire","content_concise":"990→  enumerates is driven by its own fixture, and each fixture asserts that `reason` ends with\n  exactly one `kind=<kind>` whose value is in the design's closed list (FR-4 §\"Every deny carries\n  a kind\"); a deny path with no fixture, or a kind outside the list, fails the AC.\n- **AC-5.1:** The wiring check emits each `UNWIRED` reason from its own fixture. `--agent agy`\n  writes no prompt and halts on each of them.\n- **AC-5.2:** Each row of FR-5's exit-code table is pinned by its own fixture, and each fixture\n  asserts the stdout token and the exit code separately:\n  - an `UNWIRED` fixture (one per reason, reusing AC-5.1's) shows check exit 0, and assembler\n    `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT agy_tdd_hook_unverified` with exit 0;\n  - a `hooks.json` ho