`NO` — and there is no `review_independence` entry with\n    `leg=6a-prime` (operator decision D-11). \"Not recorded\" must not read as \"independent\": without\n    the warning, a skipped record would hide a Codex-on-Codex self-review. The other `archreview`\n    values already surface on their own and add no `unrecorded` warning: absent or unrecognised is\n    the blocker `archreview_not_run`, `SKIPPED_NO_PANE` the blocker `archreview_skipped`, and\n    `SKIPPED_OPERATOR_OVERRIDE` the warning `archreview_overridden` — in none of them did a\n    6a-prime leg run, so there is nothing to record.\n  - **Features that predate this field.** The check applies to every feature whose Phase-7 check\n    runs after this ships, with no grandfather rule (D-11). An archived feature is unaffected: the\n    only code callers of `h_mad_phase7_preconditions.py` are its own CLI and its tests, so nothing\n    re-runs it over closed features. A feature in flight whose 6a-prime ran before the field\n    existed reaches Phase 7 with the warning; the orchestrator either adds the missing entry by\n    the **Record** mechanism above, from the 6a-prime dispatch log, or carries the warning into the\n    report.\n  - `review_independence_malformed` per FR-1.\n\n  The CLI prints each one as a `WARNING <code>: …` line, the form it already uses for every\n  warning. FR-10 makes the Phase-7 report carry them.\n\n","total_lines":1251}},"locations":[]}
{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-4cdced6c-0ee2-4ce0-9fd8-1b8d86482cfe-26","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"1017→- **AC-7.2:** `review_independence_unrecorded` fires, with no `leg=6a-prime` entry, for each\n  implementer `codex` (field absent included), `agy`, `grok` and `claude`, each from its own\n  fixture (`grok` and `claude` through `implementer_switch.to`, the only FR-1 routing field that takes them; `implementation_authors` is an authorship record and does not trigger the warning), and for each `archreview` value `READY_TO_MERGE`, `WITH_FIXES` and `NO`. It does not fire\n1020→  when a `leg=6a-prime` entry exists, nor when `archreview` is absent, `SKIPPED_NO_PANE` or\n  `SKIPPED_OPERATOR_OVERRIDE`.\n- **AC-7.3 (v1.8):** FR-7 §\"Attribution\" is pinned by fixtures, each RED against the mutant it\n  names and GREEN on the rule:\n  - **routing is not authorship:** `implementer_switch.to=agy` stored, the module's code from a\n    Codex dispatch, a Codex reviewer → `implementer=codex`, `independent=false`, and\n    `review_non_independent` fires. Mutant: attribution read from `implementer_switch.to`.\n  - **multi-author, recovered (E2):** authors agy then Codex; a grok 5e-review →\n    `implementer=codex`, `independent=true`; a Codex 5e-verify → `implementer=codex`,\n    `independent=false`; then, with the dispatch context discarded, an agy 6a-prime →\n1030→    `implementer=agy`, `independent=false`. Mutant: authors recovered from earlier entries'\n    `implementer` values only. The recovered set's source is `implementation_authors` (FR-1,\n    D-15), holding `{m, agy}` then `{m, codex}`.\n  - **pre-field feature (D-15):** the same reviews on a record with no `implementation_authors`\n    → the 6a-prime leg writes no entry for the module. Mutant: an absent field read as an empty\n    author set, so the agy reviewer reads as independent.\n  - **RED is not authorship (E4):** an agy 5d RED dispatch then a C