decision\":\"ask\"}`), agy is\n660→   told to write a production `.py` with no failing test during active step5.\n   - **Pass:** the file does not exist afterwards, and the stream-json log shows the gate's\n     reason.\n   - This step settles two unknowns: how agy combines a `deny` with a sibling `ask`, and whether\n     agy requires workspace trust for `.agents/hooks.json`. It does not settle what agy does when\n     a handler times out. An ordinary deny returns well inside the deadline, so no handler times\n     out on this step. Step 2a settles that.\n   - Until it passes, `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` stands.\n\n2a. **Forced handler timeout.** A temporary delay hook goes in the same project `.agents/hooks.json`","absolute_path":"/Users/kimhawk/.local/state/h-mad/grok-audit-surface/run-ab2c85dc2e25-20261024T132452Z/roots/gas-root-d8-s2v1-isogl9ls/docs/01-plan/features/agy-coder-fallback.spec.md","offset":640,"limit":30,"raw_output":"### FR-8 — Live tracer, and the timeout it measures\n\nOne real task is staged with `--agent agy` and dispatched headless through\n`hmad-dispatch exec agy`. Every reading goes to a committed probe under\n`docs/03-analysis/probes/agy-coder-fallback/`, stamped with the sha and with `agy --version`.\n- **Version.** This spec fixes no agy version. At `200ffd52`, `agy --version` prints `1.4.0`\n  (earlier readings in this feature saw `1.3.6`). Each FR-8 reading stamps the version it ran\n  against, and a reading taken under a different version than the gate's other readings is\n  re-taken, never carried.\n- **When it runs (D-13, operator decision on the design's OQ-B).** FR-8 is a post-merge stage: it\n  runs after Phase 7's integrate, against the gate installed from main, and the feature is recorded\n  COMPLETE only after the stage passes. Until then the feature is not COMPLETE, and\n  `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` stands.\n\n1. **Payload capture.** A temporary capture hook records one real `toolCall` per class-(b) tool\n   and per `run_command`. It establishes the arg keys FR-4 leaves open, and whether `workspacePaths`\n   is present. The capture hook is removed after use (probe-then-delete), and the probe records\n   that it was removed.\n2. **Real refusal.** With the operator's real global `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json` loaded (it\n   carries the `orca-status` `PreToolUse` `*` hook, which prints `{\"decision\":\"ask\"}`), agy is\n   told to write a production `.py` with no failing test during active step5.\n   - **Pass:** the file does not exist afterwards, and the stream-json log shows the gate's\n     reason.\n   - This step settles two unknowns: how agy combines a `deny` with a sibling `ask`, and whether\n     agy requires workspace trust for `.agents/hooks.json`. It does not settle what agy does when\n     a handler times out. An ordinary deny returns well inside the deadline, so no handler times\n     out on this step. Step 2a settles that.\n   - Until it passes, `step5:agy_tdd_hook_unverified` stands.\n\n2a. **Forced handler timeout.** A temporary delay hook goes in the same project `.agents/hooks.json`\n","total_lines":1251}},"locations":[]}
{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-4cdced6c-0ee2-4ce0-9fd8-1b8d86482cfe-28","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"1005→  `implementer_switch` it also applies `rfc3339_datetime` to `ts`, and only when `value` is a\n  `dict`: it calls `_semantic_ok({\"implementer_switch\": value})`, the same predicate `classify`\n  uses, so `None` (the schema's `[\"object\", \"null\"]`) and every other non-`dict` go to the schema\n  alone and never raise (v1.1 applied the predicate unguarded; design audit cycle 2). An entry is well-formed when\n  `property_valid(\"review_independence\", [entry])` holds **and** `entry[\"independent\"] ==\n1010→  (entry[\"reviewer\"] != entry[\"implementer\"])`. A boolean that contradicts its own two agents is\n  malformed, so it is never read as `independent=true`.\n- **`review_independence_malformed`** is emitted for each entry that is not well-formed, and once\n  when the field is present and not a list.\n- **`review_non_independent`** is emitted for each well-formed entry with `independent=false`,\n  naming the leg, the module and the agent.\n- **`review_independence_unrecorded`** is emitted when `record.get(\"archreview\")` is in\n  `{\"READY_TO_MERGE\", \"WITH_FIXES\", \"NO\"}` and no **well-formed** entry has `leg == \"6a-prime\"`.\n  - The code path has no implementer condition (D-11), and it reads neither `implementer` nor\n    `implementer_switch`, nor `implementation_authors` (an authorship record no script reads,\n1020→    spec FR-1 D-15), so AC-7.2's per-implementer fixtures (`grok` and `claude` through\n    `implementer_switch.to`) all reach the same branch.\n  - The detail text names the agents the record's entries attest (a projection, which is why it\n    is only detail text and never an author set the attribution reads): the distinct `implementer` values\n    of the well-formed 5e entries, sorted, or `authors=unrecorded` when there are none. It never\n    names `implementer_switch.to` or `implementer`: they record routing, and the same attribution\n    rule as the entries applies to every surface that names an author.\n  - A malformed 6a-prime entry does not count as recorded, so it raises both warnings.\n- Each warning prints through the existing `  WARNING <code>: <detail>` loop in `main`.\n\n1030→### FR-8 — the tracer, after the merge (DO-6, R-2) — OQ-B, spec D-13\n\n**Why after the merge.** The tracer needs agy to run the gate at the installed path,\n`~/.gemini/config/skills/h-mad/` → `/Users/kimhawk/orca/skills/h-mad`\n(`ls -la ~/.gemini/config/skills` at `29ae3e7b`). That path is main, and main gains the gate only\nwhen this feature merges. An override flag would ship a code path that points the check away from\nthe installed gate. A hand edit of the symlink would also change every live session.\n\n**The stage.** It runs after Phase 7's integrate and before the feature is recorded COMPLETE.\n1. **A fixture project.** It is a throwaway git repository with one module task. It has its own\n1040→   `docs/.bkit-memory.json` step5 record and its own `.agents/hooks.json`, holding FR-5's exact\n   entry. It is created beside this checkout, never under `/tmp`, because agy's trust decision for\n   `.agents/hooks.json` may depend on location.\n2. **Step 1, payload capture.** The real class-(b) payload keys are recorded, and so is\n   `init.tools` with `agy --version`. They land as one commit on main that fills `PATH_KEYS` and"}}],"rawOutput":{"type":"ReadFile","FileContent":{"content":"1005→  `implementer_switch` it also applies `rfc3339_datetime` to `ts`, and only when `value` is a\n  `dict`: it calls `_semantic_ok({\"implementer_switch\": value})`, the same predicate `classify`\n  uses, so `None` (the schema's `[\"object\", \"null\"]`) and every other non-`dict` go to the schema\n  alone and never raise (v1.1 applied the predicate unguarded; design audit cycle 2). An entry is well-formed when\n  `property_valid(\"review_independence\", [entry])` holds **and** `entry[\"independent\"] ==\n1010→  (entry[\"reviewer\"] != entry[\"implementer\"])`. A boolean that contradicts its own two agents is\n  malformed, so it is never read as `independent=true`.\n- **`review_independence_malformed`** is emitted for each entry that is not well-formed, and once\n  when the field is present and not a list.\n- **`review_non_independent`** is emitted for each well-formed entry with `independent=false`,\n  naming the leg, the module and the agent.\n- **`review_independence_unrecorded`** is emitted when `record.get(\"archreview\")` is in\n  `{\"READY_TO_MERGE\", \"WITH_FIXES\", \"NO\"}` and no **well-formed** entry has `leg == \"6a-prime\"`.\n  - The code path has no implementer condition (D-11), and it reads neither `implementer` nor\n    `implementer_switch`, nor `implementation_authors` (an authorship record no script reads,\n1020→    spec FR-1 D-15), so AC-7.2's per-implementer fixtures (`grok` and `claude` through\n    `implementer_switch.to`) all reach the same branch.\n  - The detail text names the agents the record's entries attest (a projection, which is why it\n    is only detail text and never an author set the attribution reads): the distinct `implementer` values\n    of the well-formed 5e entries, sorted, or `authors=unrecorded` when there are none. It never\n    names `implementer_switch.to` or `implementer`: they record routing, and the same attribution\n    rule as the entries applies to every surface that names an author.\n  - A malformed 6a-prime entry does not count as recorded, so it raises both warnings.\n- Each warning prints through the existing `  WARNING <code>: <detail>` loop in `main`.\n\n1030→### FR-8 — the tracer, after the merge (DO-6, R-2) — OQ-B, spec D-13\n\n**Why after the merge.** The tracer needs agy to run the gate at the installed path,\n`~/.gemini/config/skills/h-mad/` → `/Users/kimhawk/orca/skills/h-mad`\n(`ls -la ~/.gemini/config/skills` at `29ae3e7b`). That path is main, and main gains 